{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond","id":1289655,"title":"Please, please fix the Lunar Bond","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-19T14:46:17-08:00","id":1289655,"title":"Please, please fix the Lunar Bond","content":"This conversation has come up a couple times now on the Exalted discord server, where things are fleeting and ephemeral, and quickly drift between topics. I care about this quite a lot and would like to make it more prominently visible, so here is my plea to the devs to change how the Bond works for 3rd edition.<br /> <br /> The fundamental problem here, that I would like to see fixed, is that the Bond is presented as mechanically one-sided. Lunars are forced to develop a tie towards their Solar mate, who is not in turn forced into any feelings towards the Lunar. First and foremost, yes, this is disturbingly reminiscent of the 2e Bond. You know, the universally despised one that managed to poison the entire splat by the end of 2e's run. Now this is of course not exactly the same. There's no Lunar-Taming Leash that lets you force the Bond tie up to defining, there's (one must hope) no prominent depictions of Solars using that connection to abuse and manipulate a Lunar mate who they care nothing for. And maybe in a world where 2e never existed, it would be okay. It might have been seen as a weird quirk that Lunars are the only ones affected by the Bond, with any weird ideas that this creates awful power imbalances being the domain of wacky forum conspiracy theories. But we don't live in that world. Third edition has gone out of its way to cut out the most poisonous memes of 2e - progenitive essence means no Dragon-Blooded breeding camps! Lots of emphasis on the power and agency of the entire Exalted Host back during the First Age, so it's very distinctly not just the Solars and their unimportant minions! The fact that it would then not only fail to do something, similar to progentive essence, that actively eliminates the concept of one-sided abusive Bonds, but explicitly <i>keep </i>them, is awful. It's a concept that should be ripped out and burned, not kept more or less intact and enshrined in the rules, with the barest hint of a tacit assumption that it probably won't be done in creepy ways this time around.<br /> <br /> Beyond just the flashbacks of the 2e Bond, it's also really, really bad at doing all the things the Bond tries to do. The primary purpose of the Bond is to provide the reincarnation romance trope, and its platonic equivalents - two people who keep finding each other and feeling the same things towards each other across every lifetime. That goes both ways. The whole <i>point </i>of it is to go both ways. When the Lunar sees the Solar and feels a sudden tug of affection as their epic love is before them, reincarnated in the flesh, that Solar is supposed to feel something similar in return. If the Lunar feels sudden love for their ancient spouse, and the Solar feels absolutely nothing for this random stranger, that's not a charming tale of love stretching out across lifetimes. That's a fucked-up tale of a magically compelled stalker, who fundamentally cannot be content with leaving this other person the hell alone. Yeah, it's less creepy when you present it with non-romantic relationships, but A) it's still not good, your ancient camaraderie between two best buds still falls flat on its face if one half of that BFF pairing doesn't give a crap about the other and B) this is a romance trope. It's a romance trope in basically every reincarnated-people-meet pop culture depiction ever. The literary inspirations section cites romance tropes for how it works. The setting chapter talks about it starting from a bunch of marriages. <i>This is a romance trope. </i>If it's creepy when used for the primary thing it's supposed to do, it's been terribly implemented.<br /> <br /> And it's not just bad for Lunars. This fucking sucks if you want your Solar to engage in Bond-related activities of any kind. The epic moment when you first encounter your Lunar mate? Nothing. Nothing happens, you feel nothing, there's just one more faceless NPC you don't care about at all. Maybe, if that NPC is really persistent in stalking you, you might even form some kind of feelings for them! Completely normal, non-magical feelings, of course. Of course you'll never love your Lunar mate in the way they love you, you physically <i>cannot </i>have that same connection, the only way you can even tell they are your Lunar mate is them assuring you that it's totally true, look at how much cooler my charms are when I use them to help you out. It's flat, empty, pointless.<br /> <br /> You can describe it otherwise, of course. You can say that your Solar immediately feels something for this other person, if you want. But the rules disagree with you, and the rules mean something here. Normally I'm all for pointing out that rules =/= physics, Creation does not run on the Ex3 game engine, etc etc, but while the rules may not be literal translations of the laws of physics in Creation, they do very much reflect how the world works. Solars may not have a specific, universal technique that costs exactly two units of essence and allows them to jump a specific distance across all Solars and all situations, but it is true that Solars who are good at jumping can wield their Essence to leap to the roof of a small building in a single, easy bound. Exalted is not a generic system of rules that can be applied to any fantasy setting, it's a very deeply tied-in set of rules that depict and are shaped by a particular world. And when those rules tell you that Lunars all care for their Solar mates, and those Solars get absolutely <i>nothing </i>in turn towards their mate, that says a lot. That makes a statement about the setting, whether you want it to or not. It may not say that there are exactly three amounts that a person in Creation can care about another person, and that Lunars always feel at least one Caring Unit towards their Solar mate, but it does say that Lunars feel some kind of special, magical connection towards their Solar mate, and this connection is not reciprocal. Or at the very least, it says that whatever Solars <i>do </i>feel towards their Lunar mate, it's so small that it doesn't count as an intimacy, while the Lunar's does and always must.<br /> <br /> There are mitigating factors, yes. It doesn't have to be a tie of love, so it's not always creepy one-sided stalking or uncaring Solars abusing their devoted Lunar mates. You're allowed to say that your Lunar doesn't have a mate at all. You can convince your Solar mate to feel the same way for you via social influence, and once you do give them a tie it can be just as strong or stronger as your magically enforced one. The Solar's player is allowed to voluntarily form intimacies towards you. You can ask your ST to house rule it into a mutual thing, and there's a reasonable chance they'll agree. There are plenty of reasons why the one-sided Bond is less toxic and creepy than it could have been. Is that <i>really</i> what we're aiming for? Is 3rd edition going to be content with that as its tagline? <i>Lunars - Fangs at the Gate: Less Toxic And Creepy Than It Could Have Been. </i>I, at least, would like to see something better than that, something that's actively good instead. You don't need any mitigating factors at all if you don't start from a basic premise that's both kinda gross and a failure at doing the one thing it's meant to accomplish.<br /> <br /> So, what are the solutions to this problem? The basic premises that aren't toxic and creepy? These two:<br /> <br /> 1 - Make the Bond mutual. Solars feel a tie towards their Lunar mate, which works the same way as the Lunar's tie. Unfortunately, as has been discussed in great length during the aforementioned discord debates, this isn't an option. People feel, rightly or wrongly, that this would be bad because it would be putting important Solar rules in the Lunar book. This isn't happening, there's no point talking about it, moving on.<br /> <br /> 2 - Remove the mechanical impact of the Bond altogether. There is no tie. Lunars are not forced to feel anything for their Solar mate. All the fluff can remain, talking about how Solar and Lunar mates feel a strange sense of recognition when they see each other, and often leading into grand romances stretched out across lifetimes. That concept's already in the corebook, we're not adding any new, exclusive Solar content to the Lunar book here. The charm riders can remain - the corebook also, conveniently enough, has a Lunar mate charm rider, so there's clear precedent for having charm effects without a mechanical effect of the Bond itself, and the concept of the Solar mate is already very well established so it's not going to look weird to have the riders without any other mechanical enforcement of the Bond. But the magically compelled tie, the thing that sets up the Bond as being inequal right from the word go because Solars can't have it too, that has to go. Abandoning the inherently unequal mechanical implementation allows the Bond to become properly reciprocal, as it always should have been - needed to be, even. It becomes something that your group can use to whatever extent they like, in whatever way they like, developing intimacies as is appropriate to the story they tell rather than being told in black and white right there on the page that the Lunar feels something and the Solar feels nothing. It still even makes the Bond feel mechanically impactful, since even without a forced intimacy, the wide range of Solar mate riders scattered across Lunar charms makes it a Big Deal by the rules when you hang out with your mate.<br /> <br /> Option 2 isn't the best case scenario. Option 1 would be preferable, a mutual Bond with actual rules showing what that's meant to mean. But we're at the point where it's been decided that's not an option at all, so it's either removing the tie or living for the rest of 3rd edition with an imbalanced Bond that evokes all the gross memes from the darker side of 2e while simultaneously failing to tell the very stories it's designed to enable. I really hope we can get the acceptable compromise of option 2, rather than being stuck with all that for another entire edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":3559,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","user":"Lanaya","date":". 02-19-2019, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T14:54:21-08:00","id":1289657,"title":"","content":"Adaptation to draw power from their metaphysical circumstance is part of Lunar core themes, hence reshaping the Castes. They were altered by the Bond to draw power from it (see Charmset). Solars were not because they\u2019re not about change and adaptation.<br /> <br /> The comparison to 2E is ridiculous. If you don\u2019t want the tie, don\u2019t take the Bond. It\u2019s that simple. Absolutely nothing is forced on the character against the player\u2019s will.<br /> <br /> Making the Bond mutually binding would have had to be done in the Core book. It is too late now.<br /> <br /> Making the Bond not binding at all, thus rendering anyone who doesn\u2019t take it an idiot since it\u2019s just free power with no trade off, kills its story weight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 02-19-2019, 07:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":18}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T15:00:14-08:00","id":1289659,"title":"","content":"I agree the bond should be mutual and more then that I don't think I've ever had a ST not have the feeling of having a mate be mutual outside of cases where the Lunar was specifically trolling the Solar by hiding it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T15:06:43-08:00","id":1289661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1289659#post1289659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree the bond should be mutual and more then that I don't think I've ever had a ST not have the feeling of having a mate be mutual outside of cases where the Lunar was specifically trolling the Solar by hiding it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I\u2019s trnd to have it spark mutually too as long as the player\u2019s consent. But I get why it\u2019s too late to add that rule now, since \u201cyou can take this automatic intimacy\u201d needed to be in Solar character creation rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T15:12:22-08:00","id":1289662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond#post1289655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When the Lunar sees the Solar and feels a sudden tug of affection as their epic love is before them, reincarnated in the flesh, that Solar is supposed to feel something similar in return. If the Lunar feels sudden love for their ancient spouse, and the Solar feels absolutely nothing for this random stranger, that's not a charming tale of love stretching out across lifetimes. That's a fucked-up tale of a magically compelled stalker, <b>who fundamentally cannot be content with leaving this other person the hell alone</b></div> </div> </div> </div> The only thing the Bond enforces is a Minor Intimacy. Now, I'm not going to blame you for forgetting this -- <i>everyone</i> forgets this -- but the intensity of an Intimacy is not a matter of depth of feeling, but of frequency.<br /> <br /> This is what the corebook has to say: <i>Minor Intimacies are notable parts of your character\u2019s worldview, but only come into play when the subject of the Intimacy is directly relevant to her current situation.</i><br /> <br /> In essence, if a Lunar's mate isn't present, they won't be more than a fond memory. Anything more is the result of outside influence or player choice, same as any other Intimacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":97,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","user":"The MG","date":". 02-19-2019, 08:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":19}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T15:15:15-08:00","id":1289664,"title":"","content":"I think I get where Lanaya is coming from.<br /> <br /> Depending how the manuscripts and final book play out, I'm tentatively planning to make the bond mutual, or to take on a life of its own, mechanically speaking.<br /> <br /> In the first case, both players would spend points equally for the bond or not at all. Or, optionally, to split the points cost - I let my players split bonus point costs for big purchases anyway. They'd have the pen to come up with how it's presented, the same way as players do for character generation.<br /> <br /> In the second, I'd treat it as a purely story element. If the players are into it, then it plays through all the benefits and drawbacks for both. Since it's introduced by the ST, it would be without points cost but I'd have a little more directorial control of how the bond is initially presented, and twists that come down the road as we play through.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In both of these cases, I believe the base assumption of this topic is that a Lunar and Solar character are both being played by players. It seems to me that the bond rules as presented assume that we're having a Lunars game and the Solar in question is an NPC. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm generally in favor of ST's taking control of how dramatic elements shape up, but I would like to hear people's thoughts on the matter!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T15:31:25-08:00","id":1289670,"title":"","content":"It doesnt even say that the intimacy has to be positive. Be that you find your Solar Bond annoying and cant wait to get away from them. Or an irrational hate. It's only as problematic as you go out of your way to make it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T15:38:32-08:00","id":1289675,"title":"","content":"Just because 2e did something horrible down a certain road doesn't mean that 3e should abandon that direction entirely - 2e had the House of Succulent Tears, and I still want there to be an Underworld; 2e had Lillun and I still want there to be Infernals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T15:42:47-08:00","id":1289677,"title":"","content":"I'm not concerned with it at all. The Lunar's get quite a few special effects via charms when dealing with their Solar mate. Also, it's a minor intimacy only. As a minor intimacy, it only matters when the Solar is directly involved with the situation. So if it's coming up in play, it's because the ST is purposely pushing the issue. Which, even without the bond's mechanics, a ST can apply any mechanical effects they need to drive a story. Furthermore their is no specified limits set on the intimacy. It could be a Tie of love, or hate, or friendship, or even annoyance! Pick any emotion you want. Lastly, not all Lunar's are required to have a Solar bond. If you are so afraid your ST will use it against you, and he's a big enough @$$ to do it when he knows you don't want it, simply declare at character creation that you're one of the Lunar's without a bond.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T15:59:54-08:00","id":1289682,"title":"","content":"I'd almost rather drop the bond personally. Like, both setting and mechanical? It adds story possibilities but it also adds expectations: that if your a Lunar your Solar mate should be a thing, should matter: Ex3 adds ways to avert this but it remains the default. GMs tend to like playing that card and while the orichalcum rule is an option in theory, there's always players like me who don't like invoking it unless we have to.<br /> <br /> So so long as we're blueskying... ditching the bond altogether would be my vote. Let Lunars be their own thing first and formost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T16:03:20-08:00","id":1289683,"title":"","content":"Rereading the rules to be honest I find your worries a bit overblown. One, it is completely optional and two the tie is a minor one of your choice as TalosX &amp; The MG have detailed. I do wish that the Solars had more interactions in their charms like Lunars do but no point in worrying about that now several years later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T16:10:53-08:00","id":1289687,"title":"","content":"I just want the Bond to be mutual. I've always liked the concept, but it's always felt weird to me that it was one sided. It's not even about the ties to previous editions, it's just more interesting of a concept to me if it goes both ways.<br /> <br /> I'll probably houserule it if it isn't changed, which should be easy enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T16:40:40-08:00","id":1289698,"title":"","content":"Just throwing this out there, guessing that folks finding this thread might find it interesting.<br /> <br /> Why would a reincarnating bond be limited to a Lunar and a Solar(oid) partnership? Could two Solars have once wed? Two Lunars? <br /> <br /> Could a DB be caught in a loop of destiny, reincarnating to seek out the Sidereal who once saved their soul from the Void?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T16:56:14-08:00","id":1289702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1289698#post1289698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just throwing this out there, guessing that folks finding this thread might find it interesting.<br /> <br /> Why would a reincarnating bond be limited to a Lunar and a Solar(oid) partnership? Could two Solars have once wed? Two Lunars? <br /> <br /> Could a DB be caught in a loop of destiny, reincarnating to seek out the Sidereal who once saved their soul from the Void?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, since reincarnation and fate are actual pillars of the setting then there is nothing preventing this kind of mythical trope.<br /> <br /> But I hold that you shouldn\u2019t dilute the impact of Solar Bond by making it equal with these errant eccentricities of fate. <br /> <br /> Solar Bond is a deliberate mystical working that bound the fate of two of the most powerful groups in Creation together basically for all time. I kind of like it to have powerful resonances in the setting and mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T17:08:28-08:00","id":1289705,"title":"","content":"Solid answer!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T17:42:42-08:00","id":1289717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1289657#post1289657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Adaptation to draw power from their metaphysical circumstance is part of Lunar core themes, hence reshaping the Castes. They were altered by the Bond to draw power from it (see Charmset). Solars were not because they\u2019re not about change and adaptation.</div> </div> </div> </div>But then, the Solars died, and for all everyone knew, they would never be coming back. Going by this point, when the Lunars changed, the bond should have ended and they should have tapped into something else altogether.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T17:51:56-08:00","id":1289719,"title":"","content":"It was that last dozen solars that mucked that up. The bond was maimed, <i>almost</i> severed, but cos of those last few it hung on by a thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T18:07:23-08:00","id":1289724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond#post1289655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The primary purpose of the Bond is to provide the reincarnation romance trope, and its platonic equivalents - two people who keep finding each other and feeling the same things towards each other across every lifetime.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excellent post but I feel like this is the major issue you are running into. Now I don't know how previous editions worked cause I have only ever played 3e but so far in the edition the bond is not for romance. It was part of a peace negotiation between solars and lunars to end a war. Given how steep reparations can be in the real world it would make sense under that framework for the bond to be burdened on the weaker exalt. Which leads into the bond charms we have seen so far being designed to make lunars better servants to solars.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon","name":"Calboon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar223_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T18:12:34-08:00","id":1289725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Calboon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1289724#post1289724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Excellent post but I feel like this is the major issue you are running into. Now I don't know how previous editions worked cause I have only ever played 3e but so far in the edition the bond is not for romance. It was part of a peace negotiation between solars and lunars to end a war. Given how steep reparations can be in the real world it would make sense under that framework for the bond to be burdened on the weaker exalt. Which leads into the bond charms we have seen so far being designed to make lunars better servants to solars.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>They meant the extradiagetic reason for its inclusion, not the intradiagetic explanation for how it happened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T18:13:55-08:00","id":1289726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1289717#post1289717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But then, the Solars died, and for all everyone knew, they would never be coming back. Going by this point, when the Lunars changed, the bond should have ended and they should have tapped into something else altogether.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And they have changed a lot of ways since then - but just cutting the Bond doesn't tell a story about change like you're implying since there's no contrast with a previous state actually in the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T18:15:08-08:00","id":1289727,"title":"","content":"The lunar bond is entirely optional. How does anyone have a problem with this? This seems like it goes beyond &quot;I don't like playing with this toy so I won't play with it&quot; into &quot;I don't like playing with this toy so nobody should play with it&quot;.<br /> <br /> Lunars have been crapped on in previous editions as solar sidekicks. The new charm set reverses that by giving them a lot of agency over the relationship. I think that's cool, personally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24366-slarn","name":"Slarn!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T18:23:11-08:00","id":1289731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slarn!</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1289727#post1289727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The lunar bond is entirely optional. How does anyone have a problem with this? This seems like it goes beyond &quot;I don't like playing with this toy so I won't play with it&quot; into &quot;I don't like playing with this toy so nobody should play with it&quot;.<br /> <br /> Lunars have been crapped on in previous editions as solar sidekicks. The new charm set reverses that by giving them a lot of agency over the relationship. I think that's cool, personally.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, if anything the Solar has to fear it more, because the Lunar can use it to muck around with them. If the silver half hates the gold, the gold is SOL.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T18:23:44-08:00","id":1289732,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the bond primarily being on the lunars end makes sense in-universe on a couple of points, I feel.<br /> <br /> First of all, thematically. The (real) moon shines with light from the sun, and so it is lunars that see the bond (as an intimacy) and reflect that light (by using it to empower their charms)<br /> <br /> Secondly, the lunar exaltation has proven the more malleable of the two, in keeping with its source. The lunars are able to re-shape their castes, and alter them between incarnations. Solar exaltations, much like the sun itself, are far more constant. It makes sense that a binding would involve re-shaping the lunar exaltation to fit around the solar exaltation rather than the other way around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T18:40:32-08:00","id":1289738,"title":"","content":"The thought also occurs that the Lunar change could be even simpler - the world changes, and so do the Lunars. They did the last time; so even if there were Solar stragglers, the overwhelming current of change could have snapped the bond.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slarn!</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1289727#post1289727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The lunar bond is entirely optional. How does anyone have a problem with this? This seems like it goes beyond &quot;I don't like playing with this toy so I won't play with it&quot; into &quot;I don't like playing with this toy so nobody should play with it&quot;.<br /> <br /> Lunars have been crapped on in previous editions as solar sidekicks. The new charm set reverses that by giving them a lot of agency over the relationship. I think that's cool, personally.</div> </div> </div> </div>2e made them compulsory sidekicks. The 1e rules were terrible*, but there was no hint of anything like 2e Solar Bond; even the Eternal Vow merit/flaw was a one-off thing, done on an individual basis.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">*Insert typical joke about how all the Lunar Charms were great, but how the teller was confused about why almost all of them were in the Autochthohians/Alchemicals book, edition depending.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T18:46:36-08:00","id":1289740,"title":"","content":"The Lunar-Solar bond being mutual should be simple fact. It's a basic fundamental part of the trope this is meant to encompass. Even in the Epic of Gilgamesh, when Gilgamesh first laid eyes on Enkidu, he knew Enkidu was special, he knew he found someone who could walk beside him as an equal. It was an instantaneous knowledge that This Person Was Worthy in Gilgamesh's mind, not only Enkidu's.<br /> <br /> This isn't saying that we should get a dozen charms for Solars that reference their Lunar Mate, but a single line that says &quot;As a lunar with a mate, you automatically care about your solar in some way, and they you&quot; is hardly a heavy gap to bridge! It's a tiny thing that would turn this from &quot;Lunars got told to marry Solars after a war, and now always have to care about that solar&quot; to &quot;Lunars and Solars made vows as equals, and now walk with those feelings through the eternities.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> No one is saying this is Lunar Taming Leash, or turning lunars into solar's servants (except one guy who did it to defend the bond, but okay). It just doesn't match the fiction presented. The fiction says 'The bond was a mutual thing, taken in between both lunars and solars, a choice they made together under the eyes of the Heavens and Sidereals, to prevent war'. But then it presents nothing that indicates it was actually mutual. The only ones who feel the bond? Lunars. The only ones who have charms calling on the bonds? Lunars. The only ones who were at all changed by this apparently world shaking marriage-deal that is SO SPECIAL AND UNIQUE THAT NO OTHER MARRIAGE CAN EVER MATCH IT... was the Lunars.<br /> <br /> <br /> So either: The marriage wasn't actually mutual.<br /> The marriage just wasn't that special.<br /> Or... uhhh...???<br /> <br /> Is it a big deal mechanically, or does it break anything? No, of course not. But the implications in setting ruin the bond for me entirely. What should be a romantic or bromantic eternally linked together soul bond loses it's weight for me if only one side remembers it. It kills it as anything unique or special. It utterly and completely ruins the entire trope, as is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11919,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11919-kittyempress","user":"KittyEmpress","date":". 02-19-2019, 09:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11919-kittyempress","name":"KittyEmpress","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"142"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T18:49:41-08:00","id":1289741,"title":"","content":"We're probably gonna do something like this in the final draft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":18}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T20:26:25-08:00","id":1289773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1289741#post1289741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're probably gonna do something like this in the final draft.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Gonna take some particularly impressive Manipulation Charms rounding out the Changing Moon trifecta to pull me out of the pit that this statement drops me into.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T20:26:44-08:00","id":1289774,"title":"","content":"I'm very mildly surprised that there doesn't seem to be anything about Lunars forging a new Solar Bond if they don't have one already or replacing the one they do have, but considering how broad the Solar Bond is as a whole, I'm not sure you could change much without making it <i>more</i> restrictive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T20:28:42-08:00","id":1289775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1289774#post1289774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm very mildly surprised that there doesn't seem to be anything about Lunars forging a new Solar Bond if they don't have one already or replacing the one they do have</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would they?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T20:40:35-08:00","id":1289779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1289775#post1289775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why would they?</div> </div> </div> </div>Cementing an alliance with a Solar who's both alive and in their vicinity instead of one who's currently dead or on the other side of Creation doing things the Lunar doesn't care about, gaining access to powers they wouldn't normally have access to, forcibly rupturing their connection to an Abyssal or Infernal mate because murdering them every time they reincarnate is too much of a hassle, it's a decent enough plot hook, messy divorces make for good drama...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T20:49:49-08:00","id":1289782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1289779#post1289779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cementing an alliance with a Solar who's both alive and in their vicinity instead of one who's currently dead or on the other side of Creation doing things the Lunar doesn't care about</div> </div> </div> </div>{shrug} I like the weight of the ancient ceremony in the hazy past. I think reassignment at will trivialises it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">gaining access to powers they wouldn't normally have access to</div> </div> </div> </div>Thus far, the only such power I know of is the one to do with Artifacts. Everything currently out there to do with a Solar is either something that is only relevant to that Solar, or can be done without them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">forcibly rupturing their connection to an Abyssal or Infernal mate because murdering them every time they reincarnate is too much of a hassle</div> </div> </div> </div>This Lunar's world view sounds crude.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T20:52:33-08:00","id":1289783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KittyEmpress</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1289740#post1289740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only ones who feel the bond? Lunars. The only ones who have charms calling on the bonds? Lunars. The only ones who were at all changed by this apparently world shaking marriage-deal that is SO SPECIAL AND UNIQUE THAT NO OTHER MARRIAGE CAN EVER MATCH IT... was the Lunars.<br /> <br /> <br /> So either: The marriage wasn't actually mutual.<br /> The marriage just wasn't that special.<br /> Or... uhhh...???<br /> <br /> Is it a big deal mechanically, or does it break anything? No, of course not. But the implications in setting ruin the bond for me entirely. What should be a romantic or bromantic eternally linked together soul bond loses it's weight for me if only one side remembers it. It kills it as anything unique or special. It utterly and completely ruins the entire trope, as is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see it as being in the same boat as how Lunars being the only ones capable of changing or choosing their own Castes doesn't make the Castes of other Exalted trivial and irrelevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T20:57:34-08:00","id":1289785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1289782#post1289782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> {shrug} I like the weight of the ancient ceremony in the hazy past. I think reassignment at will trivialises it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hence why I'm only very mildly surprised that it can't be reassigned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T21:05:32-08:00","id":1289789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KittyEmpress</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1289740#post1289740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...No one is saying this is Lunar Taming Leash...</div> </div> </div> </div>I will - we're like ~200 words away from Sun and Moon Method showing up again. Just have something that makes the minor tie defining and incredibly difficult to erode and we're back in business.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2154-cactuar","name":"Cactuar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2154_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T21:09:53-08:00","id":1289792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cactuar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1289789#post1289789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I will - we're like ~200 words away from Sun and Moon Method showing up again.</div> </div> </div> </div>What are you basing this on?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T21:14:09-08:00","id":1289794,"title":"","content":"Alright, I promised on the Discord to write something out when I was home and could do a long, coherent argument. So I will! As preamble, note I don't think it's actually a big deal if you *do* go for a reciprocated bond. But much like I'll argue that BP isn't actually a design mistake necessarily, I can argue for the 3e version of the Bond quite well.<br /> <br /> The Bond, as presented, has absolutely nothing to do with Solars except insofar as they (and Abyssals, and Infernals) are the objects of it. But the Bond itself <i>is not a Solar thing</i>.<br /> <br /> It is the double-edged sword the Lunars installed in themselves to keep the Solars in check. It is, in implementation and in setting, the precise opposite of the hidden glowing weak spot a Solar could hit for massive damage. The Bond does not demand the Lunar love the Solar, it demands only that they <i>feel</i>. As the Dionysian counterpart to the Apollonian Solars, that's entirely appropriate.<br /> <br /> The Lunar charms we've seen make the Bond both a valuable help when assisting a Solar the Lunar approves of, and a deadly weapon when harming a Solar they do not. What it isn't is the 2nd edition weakness. As such, I believe it should be evaluated as presented currently, and not as you might think of it. (That said, I would be highly surprised if one of the Lunar Manipulation charms do not allow them to instill an intimacy in their bonded Solar.)<br /> <br /> This is, of course, besides the practical aspects of having Solar-pertaining rules retrofitted into the core via a supplement, or the setting detail that not ever Lunar is bonded, and not every bonded Lunar is liable to ever meet their bonded Solar. My point is in 3e, demanding that Solars be affected by the bond in more than a few weakpoints in charms strikes me like demanding that Solars ought to be able to shapeshift a little.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T21:22:55-08:00","id":1289796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aliasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1289794#post1289794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the Bond itself <i>is not a Solar thing</i>.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea of Lunars experiencing their side of that connection as they do because of the significance of raw emotion to their overall ethos, both in feeling and inflicting it, and in the mutability of their Essence. And even then, no more than to the degree that a Minor Tie entails, barring relevant character interaction.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of Solars experiencing their side of it partially on the strength of past life memories (which not all Solars experience to the same degree, and the last I understood a lot of people preferred it that way), and primarily on the strength of being around a Lunar being a Lunar for more than five minutes.<br /> <br /> I'm sure that once we see what the Full and No Moon Castes can do, they'll be capable of conducting themselves in all kinds of ways that compel strong emotions from a Solar.<br /> <br /> I think that a lot of Solars who spend a week around a Changing Moon Caste and aren't very heavily invested in Integrity might end up clinging around their knees, wondering how they ever got so lucky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T21:27:34-08:00","id":1289799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1289792#post1289792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What are you basing this on?</div> </div> </div> </div>The word count of Sun and Moon Method. To my recollection, prior to Glories there weren't any charms that exploited the bond in that manner. There was no way to give a Lunar a bond of 5, it was entirely voluntary on the Lunar players' part.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2154-cactuar","name":"Cactuar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2154_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T21:33:05-08:00","id":1289801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1289657#post1289657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Adaptation to draw power from their metaphysical circumstance is part of Lunar core themes, hence reshaping the Castes. They were altered by the Bond to draw power from it (see Charmset). Solars were not because they\u2019re not about change and adaptation.<br /> <br /> The comparison to 2E is ridiculous. If you don\u2019t want the tie, don\u2019t take the Bond. It\u2019s that simple. Absolutely nothing is forced on the character against the player\u2019s will.<br /> <br /> <u>Making the Bond mutually binding would have had to be done in the Core book. It is too late now.</u><br /> <br /> Making the Bond not binding at all, thus rendering anyone who doesn\u2019t take it an idiot since it\u2019s just free power with no trade off, kills its story weight.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree, so long as they make it clear that not all solars have a bonded lunar mate and its therefore a <i>completely optional</i> rule set I don't see why they couldn't add a solar side to the bond somewhere besides the corebook. It would only be an issue if every single solar has a bond mate unlike lunars who don't all have one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T21:59:15-08:00","id":1289808,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m not sure this helps enough, but there is at least one solar charm (Stubborn Boar Defense, p.303 core book) that takes the bond into consideration and gives a weakness to the Solar and an advantage to the Lunar (I can\u2019t remember if there are any more than that. Not a Solar expert, sorry)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1920-kim","name":"Kim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T21:59:43-08:00","id":1289809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cactuar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1289799#post1289799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The word count of Sun and Moon Method.</div> </div> </div> </div>The word count of Sun and Moon Method was created ten years ago, by a person who not only ultimately kind of disavowed it, but has not been a writer for the current line in about two years.<br /> <br /> Unless you're worried at the possibility of a time-travelling Holden being given a writing gig and no developer oversight, I do not believe that the fear of such a Charm being written again is justified.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T22:47:00-08:00","id":1289818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cactuar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1289799#post1289799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The word count of Sun and Moon Method. To my recollection, prior to Glories there weren't any charms that exploited the bond in that manner. There was no way to give a Lunar a bond of 5, it was entirely voluntary on the Lunar players' part.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>... So... Don't let anybody make it? Keep a Design Guide on tap that says &quot;BTW don't do THAT again&quot; and if anybody tries to submit a Charm like that, Vance and Minton just slash it through with a big red X and writes &quot;No&quot; next to it?<br /> <br /> &quot;Someone, Somewhere, by going against the spirit and design idea of this mechanic could use it in an exploitative way&quot; shouldn't be the grounds for throwing everything out ever. Maybe keep in mind and patch slightly, but no reason to throw out the entire house's plumbing because the sink could theoretically back up and explode.<br /> <br /> Reminds me of when Arms was in development, and someone suggested &quot;Hey what about like, a Warstrider with Intimacies, like 'I Fight To Protect The Weak'?&quot; as an idea. There was one person who flat-out called it Bad Design (yes they went that far) because, they insisted, that if you do that then EVERY GM will make it so that EVERY Warstrider will have Intimacies, and all those Intimacies will be &quot;Solar Exalts (Blinding Hatred)&quot; just so the Warstrider will attack any PC group that finds it.<br /> <br /> As Isator pointed out, Holden is unlikely to contribute to Exalted again. So the odds of someone writing another Sun and Moon Method in official work is slim, at best. Then that will need to get past Vance and Minton, neither of whom seem keen on letting the Bond be what it was in 2e.<br /> <br /> Let's be honest, the kind of people who would WANT to make Sun and Moon Method at their table probably aren't the types to use it anywhere BUT at their tables, and it's not going to get heavy approval outside of those tables. This feels more than a little alarmist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T23:08:48-08:00","id":1289823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aliasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1289794#post1289794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lunar charms we've seen make the Bond both a valuable help when assisting a Solar the Lunar approves of, and a deadly weapon when harming a Solar they do not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which of the previewed Charms are people thinking of when they talk about this ambivalence? (Soul-Baring Testament and Creation-Spanning Passion, I guess? The Lunar can also, I suppose, champion customs the Solar is trying to reform?)<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T23:36:51-08:00","id":1289831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1289823#post1289823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which of the previewed Charms are people thinking of when they talk about this ambivalence? (Soul-Baring Testament and Creation-Spanning Passion, I guess? The Lunar can also, I suppose, champion customs the Solar is trying to reform?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Putting aside &quot;most of them&quot;, since obviously a Lunar can act against a Solar the same way as anyone... Yes, Soul-Bearing Testament is a good way to tell other people that Solar sure is a jerk, assuming the Lunar's bond-Tie takes that form. Shining Moon-Child Mark has no cost when used against a Solar mate, and &quot;a crippling injury&quot; is one of the ways you can mark someone. Silver Soul Conviction likewise only cares that the intimacy is upheld. Creation-Spanning Passion certainly has a 'negative' use, yes.<br /> <br /> Still, that's four charms that can unambiguously be used with negative Ties granted by a Solar Bond turned bad, which isn't too bad.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T23:46:48-08:00","id":1289833,"title":"","content":"In the absence of specific mechanics, past-life flash-backs are an excellent canon-supported way to have that mutual moment of recognition and connection when a Solar and Lunar bond-pair meet, if that's something the player or ST wants to do.<br /> <br /> My primary problem with Solar Bond as presented is that for no reason I can discern, the text constrains all Solar-Lunar pairings to having originated with an arranged marriage, which makes me viscerally uncomfortable. That's just not very romantic. Neither is it very platonic. It's like the worst of both worlds. It just makes the story of the bond more political than spiritual. I guess the intent was to make the bond mutually consensual, and give players more agency over whether this story element comes into play for their character, which is definitely good, but the execution just presents different problems, one of which is, ironically, player agency.<br /> <br /> Maybe a lot of people won't care about the origin of their bond, and it certainly doesn't dictate how the pair relates to each other now, but what if I <i>wanted</i> to specify the origins of my reincarnating power-couple as anything other than this one narrative we've been given? What if I wanted to tell literally any other story about the relationship that led their fates to intertwine? Why are those stories off the cards? If the bond needs to be the result of a singular effort to tie the Solars and Lunars together (and I guess I don't have a problem with a peace deal being the impetus for that), why did they only decide to sanctify this alliance with marriages? I mean, what happened to all the Solars and Lunars at the time who were asexual/aromantic or just, you know, already happily married to someone else, like a mortal? Did they just not get to participate in this whole eternal-soul-union thing, even if they wanted to participate in some other way, by swearing oaths as blood-siblings or something?<br /> <br /> &quot;Sorry honey, I love you, but we gotta divorce or I'm going to miss out on having a soul-mate <i>for all of time</i>, so I'm ditching you to marry my best friend. No, we can't just swear to be BFFs. Gotta get hitched. It's a whole thing.&quot;<br /> <br /> I know it's easy to golden-rule this, but because it's so easy (ie, nothing seems to break by changing it), I don't see the reason for the restriction in the first place.<br /> <br /> Edited to say: I'm otherwise loving the Lunar previews. I don't want the fact that the Solar bond is all I've talked about in relation to Lunars so far to give the impression that I'm not hyped for this book. It's just one thing that's bringing me down in a sea of very awesome things that are giving me joy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":23907,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","user":"Measure of Hope","date":". 02-20-2019, 02:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T00:17:58-08:00","id":1289838,"title":"","content":"I honestly just tend to assume the number of bonds is less than the number of marriages - either because some of the symbolic marriages did not result in a bond or because some intervening event dissolve the bond (the moon is, after all, notoriously fickle.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aliasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1289831#post1289831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Putting aside &quot;most of them&quot;, since obviously a Lunar can act against a Solar the same way as anyone..</div> </div> </div> </div>This would apply equally to the Charm sets of any Exalt with an Intimacy of any type towards the Solar, yes? I wasn't trying to put you on the spot, but this kind of defensive rhetorical chaff doesn't lend much weight to your arguments.<br /> <br /> Your actual examples are fine, and I mostly agree with them, though Soul-Baring Testament lowers a subject's Resolve against the Solar (making it less than ideal for a smear campaign if your target is in any way armed to speak in their own defense) and Creation-Spanning Passion is bidirectional (making a Solar hate you and then arming them to track you is <i>probably </i>a deadly weapon, but deadly to <i>whom</i>?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":1653,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","user":"Five Eyes","date":". 02-20-2019, 03:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T00:53:08-08:00","id":1289841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1289838#post1289838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This would apply equally to the Charm sets of any Exalt with an Intimacy of any type towards the Solar, yes? I wasn't trying to put you on the spot, but this kind of defensive rhetorical chaff doesn't lend much weight to your arguments.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite so, but I wouldn't call it chaff. Not in the face of a couple of editions of &quot;SOLARS ALWAYS <b>ALWAYS</b> WIN!&quot; being a fairly common assumption in the fanbase, and Lunars getting the butt of it for a good chunk of those two editions. It doesn't hurt to remind people that &quot;The Solars get to play Exalted on Easy Mode&quot; isn't the same as &quot;always win&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your actual examples are fine, and I mostly agree with them, though Soul-Baring Testament lowers a subject's Resolve against the Solar (making it less than ideal for a smear campaign if your target is in any way armed to speak in their own defense) and Creation-Spanning Passion is bidirectional (making a Solar hate you and then arming them to track you is <i>probably </i>a deadly weapon, but deadly to <i>whom</i>?) </div> </div> </div>So don't use Soul-Baring Testament in the presence of your Solar. (Although you're right, as written it's a weakness of the charm specifically against that Solar.) And yes, CSP is bidirectional, but the Lunar is almost certainly better equipped for hiding and harrying at a distance.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T01:40:39-08:00","id":1289847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cactuar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1289799#post1289799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The word count of Sun and Moon Method. To my recollection, prior to Glories there weren't any charms that exploited the bond in that manner. There was no way to give a Lunar a bond of 5, it was entirely voluntary on the Lunar players' part.</div> </div> </div> </div>The bond's impact on MoEP: Lunars is actually more insidious.<br /> My understanding is that at the start of 2e, the assuption was that Desus and Lilith began in a marriage of equals that was gradually corrupted by the Great Curse, Desus slowly went crazy and Lilith was powerless to rein him in (iirc that's the characterisation from the novels). This informed Lunar mental defences and a notable weakness against UMI from non-Creatures of Darkness.<br /> <br /> DotFA really dialed back on the nebulous corruption aspect of the Great Curse and made it a mirror for your worst faults. It's one of the few things it did right, but it utterly threw Desus under the bus. This Lilith didn't say no to him because she's never been his equal and he's been micromanaging her to some extent since they first met.<br /> <br /> Basically, what I'm saying is that Sun and Moon Method was the least of their problems.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T01:45:49-08:00","id":1289848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1289847#post1289847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The bond's impact on MoEP: Lunars is actually more insidious.<br /> My understanding is that at the start of 2e, the assuption was that Desus and Lilith began in a marriage of equals that was gradually corrupted by the Great Curse, Desus slowly went crazy and Lilith was powerless to rein him in (iirc that's the characterisation from the novels). This informed Lunar mental defences and a notable weakness against UMI from non-Creatures of Darkness.<br /> <br /> DotFA really dialed back on the nebulous corruption aspect of the Great Curse and made it a mirror for your worst faults. It's one of the few things it did right, but it utterly threw Desus under the bus. This Lilith didn't say no to him because she's never been his equal and he's been micromanaging her to some extent since they first met.<br /> <br /> Basically, what I'm saying is that Sun and Moon Method was the least of their problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was more of a symptom of the attitude. Which was rather obnoxious, that if you weren't a solar you couldn't ever match for even a second.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T02:04:18-08:00","id":1289850,"title":"","content":"Giving both members of the pairing a minor intimacy of their choice seems like an easy change that would address these concerns, and indeed, making it two-way does seem to play more into a well-known trope and put more focus on it as either a wholesome and welcome thing, or a potential source for tragedy. I am hoping for a positive example with the signature characters actually, because, yes, the focus on Lilith and Desus, without much in the way of counter-examples is without a doubt responsible for most of this mess. Showing us an epic, age-spanning romance which uplifts the people involved this time around could be the best cure.<br /> <br /> (Imho, even better would be to open up this merit, in a 'light' version, to all reincarnating exaltations, with the addition that it is most common in solar-lunar pairings, and perhaps leaving the actual charm support mostly for that particular combination to give that mechanical weight.)<br /> <br /> That said, having actually played a Lunar with Solar Bond 5 in 2e, its negative rep is overblown. You could define how you feel about your Solar back then as well, and the bonuses were also very much about supporting them to be what you, the Lunar, wanted them to be. It <i>really </i>did not turn you into some sort of subservient slave who could not disagree or take the lead. In fact the penalties were, in the context of the 2e social system, fairly trivial in the end. If both partners knew the other well beating each others' social defense was a given anyway! It would be the Solar's or Lunar's nature and Charms that could turn the relationship skeevy and abusive, <b><i>not the Solar Bond</i></b>. Desus was a manipulative, abusive pos, and armed with the nastiest of mindbender Charms. Any Solar who is so inclined could do it to anyone, but so could the Lunar. Their charm set had issues, sure, but was solid enough on the social front to also be a total creep.<br /> <br /> Of course, going there in your rp is... well, rarely welcomed, and also not constrained to Solar Bonds or even Exalted, and nothing in the description of Solar Bond <i>forces </i>you or makes a Desus/Lilith outcome the default one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1550,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","user":"Angwe","date":". 02-20-2019, 08:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T03:52:50-08:00","id":1289863,"title":"","content":"One thing I think making the bond one-sided does is that it allows lunars to approach their mate on their own terms. A big thing was made about the lunars trying to move on from the solars and them not being sure what to to about their return. Their mates feeling as strong a pull and seeking them out could go badly.<br /> <br /> Also I do think that feeling the intimacy and developing charms are intrinsically linked. To say the solars feel it without being able to grab hold and build on it seems... counter-intuitive. Like it's just sat there, flapping in the breeze.<br /> <br /> I dunno, maybe you could design a charm tree that lets them strengthen and build on it. It feels like something the solar would need to <i>want</i> to do, and probably need to have their lunar there helping them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T07:58:17-08:00","id":1289926,"title":"","content":"I don't see why EQUALITY in a relationship that even people defending a one sided bond ITT have admitted was a relationship between equals is that hard to understand. It's not a relationship between equals if only one person feels it, or cares about it. It's just innately not. Like 100%, that is not the definition of between equals. It is the exact opposite.<br /> <br /> You cannot argue 'this is between equals', while this is built on a fundamental inequality being defended for no reason other than 'I don't want my solar to have to care about some lunar'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11919-kittyempress","name":"KittyEmpress","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"142"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T08:02:57-08:00","id":1289928,"title":"","content":"What about 'I don't want some solar to have to care about my lunar'? As a Lunar player the lopsided nature of the bond is a point of attractiveness to me, whereas as a Solar player I couldn't care much for it either way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25050-fodor","name":"FODOR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T08:23:04-08:00","id":1289936,"title":"","content":"My thoughts on why no new Bonds or why there aren't Lunar Bonds wiht other Exalts is that it's probably just a weird synergy thing. I think it's notable that in Creation, unlike a lot of Earth cultures, the Sun and Moon while top dogs, aren't quite &quot;paired&quot; often. They overlap, but it's more just due to them being the kind of gods they are than some built-in-pairing. The Solar and Lunar Exalted just happened to have some synergy to them beyond their deities and that's what I tend to think the Bond as: An unforseen outgrowth that happened to affect both Exaltations. As for why no new Bonds, my other thought is time. It wasn't one lifetime that forged the gbonds, but a few of htem. WHich is why also some Lunars or Solars might not have one: Even if they got married in the first generaiton, it might have just not been maintained beyond the intial thing and so no synergy was built-up.<br /> <br /> As to the mutual-or-not, I don't see why it's a big deal to just make it that. And why the corebook needs to be errata'd really. The Bond is described for what it needs to be in most Solar games in the corebook. That there's an option for a Solar to also have the Bond that happens to be in the book of the Exalts they have Bonds with (which also require the Solar urles anyhow), I don't see the issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T08:30:48-08:00","id":1289939,"title":"","content":"The Lunar-Solar Bond is something I always think will be cool, and ends up being mostly not very relevant, even with Solar Bond 5. It has some effect conceptually (the unrequited love*, the bond of brotherhood, etc), but not mechanically.<br /> <br /> *The unrequited and thus tragic love is, I assume, Fodor's point.<br /> <br /> On my Lunar with Solar Bond 5, I don't believe I ever used my 10 bonus dice, or took the -5 penalty to MDV, because it's not like his Solar Mate used social attacks on his circle-mate.<br /> <br /> It did make a roleplaying difference, but roleplaying is kind of up to the players anyway.<br /> <br /> Perhaps, with the right charms, it'll have more mechanical heft.<br /> <br /> I do see KittyEmpress's point about the unfairness (though it would still be unfair if the Solar had a Tie of &quot;They're annoying&quot; and the Lunar &quot;I love them!&quot; Or vice-versa). But honestly, the mechanical effect of the Solar Bond, unless you take charms, is so irrelevant that it doesn't make much difference.<br /> <br /> (Honestly, I kind of feel Solar Bonds might be more fitting for a Solar-Solar relationship, but I guess Solar-Lunar is more interesting.)<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T08:40:29-08:00","id":1289945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Measure of Hope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1289833#post1289833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe a lot of people won't care about the origin of their bond, and it certainly doesn't dictate how the pair relates to each other now, but what if I <i>wanted</i> to specify the origins of my reincarnating power-couple as anything other than this one narrative we've been given? What if I wanted to tell literally any other story about the relationship that led their fates to intertwine? Why are those stories off the cards? If the bond needs to be the result of a singular effort to tie the Solars and Lunars together (and I guess I don't have a problem with a peace deal being the impetus for that), why did they only decide to sanctify this alliance with marriages? I mean, what happened to all the Solars and Lunars at the time who were asexual/aromantic or just, you know, already happily married to someone else, like a mortal? Did they just not get to participate in this whole eternal-soul-union thing, even if they wanted to participate in some other way, by swearing oaths as blood-siblings or something?<br /> <br /> &quot;Sorry honey, I love you, but we gotta divorce or I'm going to miss out on having a soul-mate <i>for all of time</i>, so I'm ditching you to marry my best friend. No, we can't just swear to be BFFs. Gotta get hitched. It's a whole thing.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I got the impression that they were using the term &quot;marriage&quot; in a much broader context than you are using here. Or rather, the term they use is &quot;political marriage,&quot; so consider how that concept differs from what you're thinking of as marriage. It's more of a formal joining of two political entities, an alliance of sorts, that neither requires or expects a romantic relationship. As far as what happens if you were already happily married? Well as in a number of the sources that Exalted draws inspiration from, when you're a god-king, you can have as many spouses as you like, with lovers and concubines on the side. The exact nature of your relationships and how you make it all work out is still up to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/91-wandering","name":"Wandering","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar91_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T09:01:08-08:00","id":1289956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KittyEmpress</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1289926#post1289926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see why EQUALITY in a relationship that even people defending a one sided bond ITT have admitted was a relationship between equals is that hard to understand. It's not a relationship between equals if only one person feels it, or cares about it. It's just innately not. Like 100%, that is not the definition of between equals. It is the exact opposite.</div> </div> </div> </div>Surely the members of a relationship can <i>be</i> equals without being <i>symmetrically invested </i>the relationship?<br /> <br /> And I think the above opinions re: the bond making sense in context have been more intellectually honest than...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KittyEmpress</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1289926#post1289926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'I don't want my solar to have to care about some lunar'.</div> </div> </div> </div>... and you do everyone involved a disservice by presuming otherwise. I get the distinct impression that you have one <i>very specific</i> idea of what trope you want the bond to be, rather than letting it be its own thing unique to this context, game, and setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T09:11:40-08:00","id":1289961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KittyEmpress</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1289926#post1289926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see why EQUALITY in a relationship that even people defending a one sided bond ITT have admitted was a relationship between equals is that hard to understand. It's not a relationship between equals if only one person feels it, or cares about it. It's just innately not. Like 100%, that is not the definition of between equals. It is the exact opposite.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that the closeness in stature between Lunars and Solars is undermined just from the impact that in conferred by a Minor Tie, and the closeness of the stature means that a Lunar can get a lot of latitude in how to handle that, whether it be preventing it from distracting or deterring them, or the manner in which they present themselves to the Solar and cultivate the ensuing relationship.<br /> <br /> I actually see the Bond as it currently is placing a lot of the agency with the Lunar, and not just from how they get a number of Charms to do things to or for the Solar with it, but because it puts them in the position to make the first move, to control the context, the freedom to forge the Solar's perception of them as they please.<br /> <br /> Or, indeed, largely disregard them; a Solar not feeling anything immediate gives the Lunar who wants to put the Bond to the back of their mind greater freedom to go off and do their own thing.<br /> <br /> And for the Lunar who does want to do those things, the kinds of powers that they have can give them a lot of latitude in how they want to shape that narrative.<br /> <br /> They're probably about as equal as two kinds of Exalted could be, but they're still extremely different. I find making it a thing that most heavily belongs to the Lunars helps to characterize that difference, as well as general control over the subject.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KittyEmpress</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">being defended for no reason other than 'I don't want my solar to have to care about some lunar'.</div> </div> </div> </div>A statement like this makes me fear that discussion is facing an uphill battle against people who are not only uninterested in hearing alternative reasons but are determined to perceive the other viewpoints in some of the worst ways possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T09:19:00-08:00","id":1289963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1289956#post1289956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Surely the members of a relationship can <i>be</i> equals without being <i>symmetrically invested </i>the relationship?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes... but they can't be equals if one isn't invested in the relationship at all.<br /> <br /> Although in practice, it's not all that difficult to give a Solar a minor intimacy if the Lunar's hanging around a lot. Just try again and again in different scenes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-20-2019, 12:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T09:19:21-08:00","id":1289964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1289956#post1289956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">letting it be its own thing unique to this context, game, and setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, while the reincarnation romance trope is part of its inspiration, and the Bond systemizes a manner in which it can play out, I think that making it the start and stop of the subject would be limiting both on the grounds of Exalted often taking these classical elements and putting a spin on them to make it their own, but would end up rather samey if they were imagined as playing out in the same way for three hundred different couples.<br /> <br /> I've no objection to something like adding a sidebar stating that there will be Solars whose past life memories are vivid enough that encountering their Mate prompts the formation of a Tie, or even Solars like the one from the comic whose memories form compelling visions of prior relationships that drive them before they even meet the Lunar. I just prefer it to not be standardised across Solars, because I like it as something proprietary to Lunars, and I like the idea that in many or most cases the Lunar gets to be the one who defines how the Solar will perceive them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T09:22:31-08:00","id":1289966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1289963#post1289963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes... but they can't be equals if one isn't symmetrically invested in the relationship at all.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I guarantee that at least three different definitions of the term &quot;equal&quot; are floating around behind the scenes of this thread, and in the absence of effective qualifiers (and people willing to consider them) there's going to be a lot of takes to the effect of accusing folks of wanting Lunars to be subordinated to Solars.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T09:30:17-08:00","id":1289968,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's the other thing. You don't want your solar to be able to just dismiss the lunar.<br /> <br /> Well then Don't. Fucking. Let. Them.<br /> <br /> Confront them. Make yourself unforgettable.<br /> <br /> Control that first impression and make sure they get the tie towards you that you want. I don't want something stupid like meeting on opposite sides of a fight to permanently sour the relationship. <br /> <br /> If you want to give lunars agency maybe you should <i>stop trying to take their agency. </i><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T09:38:07-08:00","id":1289973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1289725#post1289725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They meant the extradiagetic reason for its inclusion, not the intradiagetic explanation for how it happened.</div> </div> </div> </div>Extradiegetic reasons was Calboon's point I think. The solar bond's new &quot;origin story&quot; being now about a marriage of convenience seems to be more about forced cooperation and/or responsibility/surveillance rather than forced love and/or friendship. Love, friendship, rivalry, hatred, mentorship, etc. mostly being the way this forced coop and responsibility thing express itself for each individual lunar rather than the actual thing in this new context.<br /> Now, the lunar rather than being about eternal love beyond death seems to be more about recurring mythological contrasting duos, as if Gilgamesh and Enkidu tie were always reincarnating with those two but not their personalities nor the nature of their relationship, the next time becoming Achylleus and Patroclos, another time Marvel's Loki and Thor, etc (Gilgamesh and Enkidu fit so much, it's so strange), which permits more diverse relationship, be it archetypal or not while not impeding any person willing to use it as a reincarnating BFF or LI trope either.<br /> Now when I think about Solar bond I think of the Lunar as the one who is the first willing to take the responsibility of killing or warring against his or her corrupted or antagonistic solar be it a friend or an enemy, the one who will make a responsibility to give help during his or her solar friend virtue flaw, the one who will advise the bonded solar on a complex and nuanced moral struggle, and lots of other things but in none of them I see love, friendship nor love-hate relationship as a necessary thing and I see now a ground for more diverse relationships than before and more thematically tied to the monster-trickster's and mythological duos mythos ones too.<br /> <br /> <br /> Angwe, Lionness, Elfive and Isator just took the words right out of my mouth with each of their posts in the 4th and 5th pages. When I started to read the topic I was like, &quot;Ow... It will take a huuuuuuge amount of time answering to everything I want to.&quot; And now I'm like &quot;Erf, nothing's left to bring any interesting thing here.&quot; ^^<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1289863#post1289863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I think making the bond one-sided does is that it allows lunars to approach their mate on their own terms. A big thing was made about the lunars trying to move on from the solars and them not being sure what to to about their return. Their mates feeling as strong a pull and seeking them out could go badly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm mostly speaking with my emotions here, but I also think it paradoxically makes the whole thing healthier than a mutual bond most of the time. Thinking about pre-usurpation cursed solars in a mutual bond makes me think about lots of unbearable things for my games whiwh still apply in later era. Late first age ancient solars just being terrifying hubristic decadent god-kings is more than enough for me.<br /> <br /> I may be okay with the mutual bond thing but not if the solars feels it the same way lunar does and if it works the same way for both. Partly for the reasons I expressed in the first paragraph andfor other reasons I feel hardly capable to express, maybe arbitrary ones in fact. ^^'<br /> I'm still completely okay with widening the solar bond merit possibilities into a more universal merit about past life tie which permits a wider amount of things and relationship than just the solar bond, like a lunar bond for some willing solar players.<br /> <br /> I hope it's not awful to read, I'm not used to forums and I'm still learning to speak english.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I'm sorry for those I may be repeating but I haven't wholly read the first, the third nor the second pages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23607,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23607-roseplancton","user":"RosePlancton","date":". 02-20-2019, 12:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23607-roseplancton","name":"RosePlancton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T09:45:53-08:00","id":1289976,"title":"","content":"Basically how I see it now is that the lunars who set up the bond were playing 4D chess. Anything about it that seems to be in the Solars favour? Actually benefits Lunars somehow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T09:52:56-08:00","id":1289980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RosePlancton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1289973#post1289973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I hope it's not awful to read, I'm not used to forums and I'm still learning to speak english.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your post is not only perfectly legible, but also quite articulate.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T10:21:33-08:00","id":1289992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1289968#post1289968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that's the other thing. You don't want your solar to be able to just dismiss the lunar.<br /> <br /> Well then Don't. Fucking. Let. Them.<br /> <br /> Confront them. Make yourself unforgettable.<br /> <br /> Control that first impression and make sure they get the tie towards you that you want. I don't want something stupid like meeting on opposite sides of a fight to permanently sour the relationship.<br /> <br /> If you want to give lunars agency maybe you should <i>stop trying to take their agency. </i><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like to subscribe to your newsletter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T10:38:28-08:00","id":1290002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1289980#post1289980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your post is not only perfectly legible, but also quite articulate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. I put so much effort into it. It really makes me happy. ^^<br /> I'm now having a silly smile and being excessively proud of my progess in english.<br /> (But at the same time I just discovered the word legible reading your post and I feel a little bit ridiculous about feeling myself so proud. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23607-roseplancton","name":"RosePlancton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T10:41:50-08:00","id":1290003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond#post1289655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1 - Make the Bond mutual. Solars feel a tie towards their Lunar mate, which works the same way as the Lunar's tie. Unfortunately, as has been discussed in great length during the aforementioned discord debates, this isn't an option. People feel, rightly or wrongly, that this would be bad because it would be putting important Solar rules in the Lunar book. This isn't happening, there's no point talking about it, moving on.<br /> <br /> 2 - Remove the mechanical impact of the Bond altogether. There is no tie. Lunars are not forced to feel anything for their Solar mate. All the fluff can remain, talking about how Solar and Lunar mates feel a strange sense of recognition when they see each other, and often leading into grand romances stretched out across lifetimes. That concept's already in the corebook, we're not adding any new, exclusive Solar content to the Lunar book here. The charm riders can remain - the corebook also, conveniently enough, has a Lunar mate charm rider, so there's clear precedent for having charm effects without a mechanical effect of the Bond itself, and the concept of the Solar mate is already very well established so it's not going to look weird to have the riders without any other mechanical enforcement of the Bond. But the magically compelled tie, the thing that sets up the Bond as being inequal right from the word go because Solars can't have it too, that has to go. Abandoning the inherently unequal mechanical implementation allows the Bond to become properly reciprocal, as it always should have been - needed to be, even. It becomes something that your group can use to whatever extent they like, in whatever way they like, developing intimacies as is appropriate to the story they tell rather than being told in black and white right there on the page that the Lunar feels something and the Solar feels nothing. It still even makes the Bond feel mechanically impactful, since even without a forced intimacy, the wide range of Solar mate riders scattered across Lunar charms makes it a Big Deal by the rules when you hang out with your mate.<br /> <br /> Option 2 isn't the best case scenario. Option 1 would be preferable, a mutual Bond with actual rules showing what that's meant to mean. But we're at the point where it's been decided that's not an option at all, so it's either removing the tie or living for the rest of 3rd edition with an imbalanced Bond that evokes all the gross memes from the darker side of 2e while simultaneously failing to tell the very stories it's designed to enable. I really hope we can get the acceptable compromise of option 2, rather than being stuck with all that for another entire edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Intimacies do not have to be mutual. They do not have to be equal. One person might be very committed to a relationship, and the other might be only vaguely attached to it. You think it's creepy that one side can love/hate another more? <i>I think it's creepy to demand love/hate from another entity, just because I currently feel love/hate.</i> And who would control the intensity? Would either of the Solar or Lunar be forced to raise its intensity when the other one did? If the Solar wants to literally force its way out of the 'friendzone' the Lunar has as its Bond Intimacy, could the Solar just flip a switch?<br /> <br /> One-sided love/hate is a perfectly valid story to tell. Unrequited love because the Solar isn't their 700+ year old self, and your slow, campaign-length goal of getting 'the original' back was a valid, almost touching, story. Lilith contemplating killing Swan when Swan barely even knew Lilith existed was one of the reasons I got interested in Bond in the first place. I want to hate somebody who doesn't hate me back, sometimes, so I can deceive them into ruining their own life or suddenly stab them in the back with them not knowing why. <i>And yes, sometimes I want to play a yandere stalker Lunar, and get sempai to notice me. It's great stress relief. </i>I want to, sometimes, explore tragic love, or build a friendship based on prior lives, and let the other guy figure it out on their own so he's not pressured. I want Lunars, definitely, to gain more mechanical benefits from how much they love/hate a Solar, than the Solar on the other end. Solars have perfection and raw excellence, let Lunars have their world-shattering emotional ties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I used to know things. Forbidden things.</b>","edited":{"userid":306,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","user":"Brasstreader","date":". 02-20-2019, 01:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/306-brasstreader","name":"Brasstreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar306_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T10:46:28-08:00","id":1290008,"title":"","content":"While I respect the point of view of those concerned with this issue, I do not share it.<br /> <br /> I'm not interested in calling Fangs or any other Ex3 product &quot;toxic&quot;. Personally I'm not offended by anything I read in an RPG book. If I don't like it, I ignore it or change it... this only gets troublesome to me when it requires me to write mechanics (which I'm not any good at), but when it is a setting element, it's completely on my hands.<br /> <br /> Again, this is not me telling anyone how they should feel about anything. You are free and intelligent enought to know your own opinions.<br /> <br /> I just wanted to add my voice to those who aren't as concerned by this topic so that the Devs can evaluate how important or not it is this whole thing for the final version of the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T11:11:40-08:00","id":1290020,"title":"","content":"Just make the bond two sided or take it away completely mechanical with the intimacy. <br /> The lore and the devs have describe it as mutual but if there is only for one it represent mechanical and only one side that get the intimacy then imo the whole War/marriage thing is not worth anything. <br /> Stick to the lore. make it mutual, both can get the intimacy. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13712-illaden","name":"Illaden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13712_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T11:18:48-08:00","id":1290024,"title":"","content":"That's what they want you to think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T11:26:58-08:00","id":1290027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illaden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290020#post1290020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just make the bond two sided or take it away completely mechanical with the intimacy.<br /> The lore and the devs have describe it as mutual but if there is only for one it represent mechanical and only one side that get the intimacy then imo the whole War/marriage thing is not worth anything.<br /> Stick to the lore. make it mutual, both can get the intimacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>The bond's already optional. It's literally only there for the players that want it.<br /> It's also one-sided only in the sense that one character gets more from it than the other. And it's shown as a good thing so far. A character with a bond will: feel it, and many of their powers are great for either helping the bondmate or screwing him over&quot;<br /> <br /> Making the bond completely symmetrical feels like a waste. And ironically bring back a little bit of the old silversolar/golden lunar problem 2e had.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T11:29:58-08:00","id":1290029,"title":"","content":"no it doesn't the whole bond is built on that both shared it, but if only one is feeling it and the other can ignore it, I don't see why it should be there as a thing. <br /> Optional if you want to play the 100 other yes,<br /> But if I wanted to play with the other 300 of course I want the solar to also feel a thing and that it is supported mechanically in the book and not only the lore. <br /> either both or none","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13712-illaden","name":"Illaden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13712_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T11:45:54-08:00","id":1290038,"title":"","content":"Again with the &quot;the other can just ignore it&quot;<br /> <br /> Did the social influence system just cease to exist while I wasn't looking?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T11:49:32-08:00","id":1290040,"title":"","content":"The Solar Bond isn't as important to Solars because they have no continuity with it. Lunars have centuries of myths, legends, and traditions tracing back to the Solar Bond and how their role in Creation changed when they lost it along with everything else. Now that Solars (plus Abyssals and Infernals) have returned to Creation, Lunars are forcibly confronted with the Solar Bond's existence and have to decide if they're going to return to the way they were in the First Age, keep doing what they're doing with the Silver Pact, or figure out a new role for themselves that may or may not account for the return of the Solars. <br /> <br /> Solars don't have any of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T11:52:33-08:00","id":1290041,"title":"","content":"Elfive. <br /> Solars doens't get a forced Intimacy like Lunars. <br /> Even if you can have it as any tie. The solar can just nope I don't have any <br /> Either both get one when they see each other or none. That is simple <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13712-illaden","name":"Illaden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13712_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T12:00:01-08:00","id":1290044,"title":"","content":"The thing about how the Bond works RAW is that it\u2019s a trade-off. The Tie for the Charm benefits.<br /> <br /> The downside of enforcing the Tie in both directions is that there\u2019s no Charm benefits for the Solar (not counting whatever benefits in the Lunar Charmset their mate chooses to extend them), and I think most of us would agree Solars are in no need of such benefits.<br /> <br /> As I said, I\u2019m all for the Tie sparking in both directions provided the player consents, but I\u2019m reluctant to enforce the Tie as inseparable from having a Lunar Mate on the Solar side since they don\u2019t get Charm benefits for it like Lunars do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T12:00:52-08:00","id":1290045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illaden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290041#post1290041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elfive.<br /> Solars doens't get a forced Intimacy like Lunars.<br /> Even if you can have it as any tie. The solar can just nope I don't have any<br /> Either both get one when they see each other or none. That is simple</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't see why it is an argument making of the mutual bond a good thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23607-roseplancton","name":"RosePlancton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T12:02:14-08:00","id":1290046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illaden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290041#post1290041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elfive. <br /> Solars doens't get a forced Intimacy like Lunars. <br /> Even if you can have it as any tie. The solar can just nope I don't have any <br /> Either both get one when they see each other or none. That is simple </div> </div> </div> </div>What\u2019s wrong with \u201cthe one that gets Charm benefits is required to take the Tie in return for said benefits; the one who has no mechanical benefits has no tie required but can opt to take one instantly upon contact if they want. Any Lunar player who doesn\u2019t want the Tie, need not take the Bond in the first place?\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 02-20-2019, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T12:18:26-08:00","id":1290052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illaden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290041#post1290041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if you can have it as any tie. The solar can just nope I don't have any</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think this is actually a thing. I mean, why would you do that? I'm not concerned about being stuck with the most boring solar on Creation. <br /> <br /> Look, can you not see the advantage lunars have here? They're disguised as a random beggar, they see their solar for the first time. Boom bond. Solar is oblivious. <br /> <br /> The lunar can then stake them out, see what they're like. Maybe jack up their appearence and pick a form suited to making a good impression, and appear to their solar as a glorious moon goddess or something. Or manipulate them into allying against their enemies and introduce themselves as someone who is <i>coincidentally</i> on the same side. <br /> <br /> The bond being one way means that when it triggers the ball is in the lunar's court. There are so many interesting stories you can spin out of that leading up til the first proper meeting. Having the solar spot them in that first scene would ruin all of that.<br /> <br /> And you can have shit like three lunars hanging round with a solar, who suspects that one of them <i>might</i> be his mate. But it doesn't matter. he and his buddies are gonna fight Prasad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T12:47:29-08:00","id":1290056,"title":"","content":"Elfive, your entire argument is predicated on the idea that 'Hey, being able to stalk your mate and force them to care about you back by spying on them with magic and then manipulating them into liking you back is totally cool, and great, and not at all skeevy and weird as fuck'.<br /> <br /> Like, you literally just described the grossest fucking idea of a 'Bond' I've ever heard of in any fiction I've ever read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11919-kittyempress","name":"KittyEmpress","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"142"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T12:52:46-08:00","id":1290060,"title":"","content":"The Lunar's <i>player </i>selects the emotional angle of the Tie, but the Lunar merely feels it immediately - and passionately, by the text. &quot;Passionate&quot; would seem to be at odds with the calculated, measured, and deliberate approach being proposed - it's a visceral emotional sensation.<br /> <br /> I feel like the Lunar would have to already have some psychological <i>stuff </i>going on if their immediate response to, say, love at first sight is &quot;I shall embark on a sustained campaign to make them amenable to and cooperative with my agenda before approaching them under false pretenses.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's not out of line for dramatic purposes (many people in plays act like that), but it seems to treat a sudden (and unbidden and inescapable) emotional response as a clinical recognition of a potential asset.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T12:59:00-08:00","id":1290066,"title":"","content":"Well, ok, not manipulating them, <i>charisma</i>-ing them. Maybe they could maneuver them into seeing the atrocities they're trying to fight and then introducing themselves. <br /> <br /> Think Morpheus in the matrix. He stalked Neo a bit before introducing himself, and that wasn't really skeevy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T12:59:45-08:00","id":1290067,"title":"","content":"If you don't like this presentation, don't use it. It's an rpg. Talk to your players. If you need to say &quot;hey don't abuse your lunar if you get one&quot;, you shouldn't be playing with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11044-kilbert","name":"kilbert","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T13:04:56-08:00","id":1290071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290066#post1290066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, ok, not manipulating them, <i>charisma</i>-ing them. Maybe they could maneuver them into seeing the atrocities they're trying to fight and then introducing themselves.<br /> <br /> Think Morpheus in the matrix. He stalked Neo a bit before introducing himself, and that wasn't really skeevy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Regardless of what Attribute you may use to do so, stalking someone to find out everything they like and care for, so you can specifically call out the ones you also like and care for, and thus ingratiate yourself to this person you are stalking is still creepy. Whether you're lying when you tell me &quot;Hey, I see you hate slavers, I also hate slavers!&quot; or telling the truth, stalking someone through the streets of Nexus and watching him, just so you can show up at the right moment to help him fight slavers and thus make him care for you is pretty skeevy and creepy.<br /> <br /> If someone followed you through your day, took down everything you liked to eat, then made sure to ambush you at lunch and be like 'omg, you like X too, I love x!' and then excused having to do so because they felt like they had an <i>inborn, innate magical connection to you</i> that you have absolutely 0 knowledge of, wouldn't you find that creepy as hell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11919-kittyempress","name":"KittyEmpress","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"142"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T13:04:57-08:00","id":1290072,"title":"","content":"Frankly, I don't think scoping out a powerful and dangerous potential ally before introducing yourself when you're in the middle of a guerrilla war is all that skeevy and not just... like... basic intelligence gathering.<br /> <br /> These people are not dating. It's a bit more complex than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 02-20-2019, 04:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T13:09:22-08:00","id":1290075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KittyEmpress</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290056#post1290056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elfive, your entire argument is predicated on the idea that 'Hey, being able to stalk your mate and force them to care about you back by spying on them with magic and then manipulating them into liking you back is totally cool, and great, and not at all skeevy and weird as fuck'.<br /> <br /> Like, you literally just described the grossest fucking idea of a 'Bond' I've ever heard of in any fiction I've ever read.</div> </div> </div> </div>Elfive did not describe a solar bond which was forced to be about stalking.<br /> And it seems that your basing your assumption on the idea that stalking is something absolutely bad rather than bad because it is most of the time in our world about persons harrassing innocent and inoffensive people. Solars are none of them. They're dangerous and this why the lunars of old tied themselves to them. The solar bond is more about &quot;monitoring&quot; beings capable to be better heroes or worse monsters than the lunars are from my point of view and because of that the solar bond is not necessarily based on relationship where equally caring is necessary for the relation to be constructive to them or the others. Those not living the relationship are more important here I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23607,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23607-roseplancton","user":"RosePlancton","date":". 02-20-2019, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23607-roseplancton","name":"RosePlancton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T13:33:11-08:00","id":1290085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KittyEmpress</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290056#post1290056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elfive, your entire argument is predicated on the idea that 'Hey, being able to stalk your mate and force them to care about you back by spying on them with magic and then manipulating them into liking you back is totally cool, and great, and not at all skeevy and weird as fuck'.<br /> <br /> Like, you literally just described the grossest fucking idea of a 'Bond' I've ever heard of in any fiction I've ever read.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I get the impression that you are really invested in the idea that the only legitimate use of the Solar Bond is for mutually-agreeable inter-incarnation romances and best-friends-forever stories, because Elfive's example is only &quot;skeevy&quot; and &quot;gross&quot; if you put taking advantage of the information asymmetry on equivalent moral footing to betrayal (or abuse, or worse) of a trusting partner.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, taken at face value, in no small part <i>because</i> the Solar isn't forced to reciprocate, it's just particular flavor of story involving someone who recognizes the Solar for who and what they once were. The particular mechanism being Lunar Feels gives you more and varied options than, say, some being who just happens to be Old Enough to personally remember a past self and perceptive enough to notice the connection, but isn't otherwise much different (morally).<br /> <br /> In any event, I feel like it's a bit of a reach to say that information asymmetry is inherently reprehensible.<br /> <br /> EDIT: or, I could have just said this: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290072#post1290072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These people are not dating.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 02-20-2019, 04:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T13:37:47-08:00","id":1290087,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I mean, what do you think Anya Silverclaw's gonna do about her Abyssal? Come clean straight up or, y'know, do some recon first?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T13:38:13-08:00","id":1290088,"title":"","content":"Okay why should lunar be the only one in something that should be mutual be like &quot;Ohh there is my solar, I get a tie now to that person&quot; while the solar can be &quot; ohh there is my lunar ohh well, I can just ignore it and no tie at all&quot; <br /> There it is the bond mechanic in clear sight how it works. <br /> WHY aren't solars getting their tie immidetly on the same premisse as the Lunar when the bond is described as something that goes both ways lore wise. <br /> Why should it just be one sided despite the lore and how devs have describe it being mutual","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13712-illaden","name":"Illaden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13712_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T13:41:10-08:00","id":1290091,"title":"","content":"&quot;Hey, so I'm the bearer of an exaltation indelibly bonded to yours millennia ago by our divine predecessors&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh. Cool story bro&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T13:41:53-08:00","id":1290092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illaden</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">despite the lore and how devs have describe it being mutual</div> </div> </div> </div>Did they? <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">/10char</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T14:32:38-08:00","id":1290100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290087#post1290087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I mean, what do you think Anya Silverclaw's gonna do about her Abyssal? Come clean straight up or, y'know, do some recon first?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, for all she knows, she should kill said Abyssal forthwith, to free the Solar Essence from this evil-crazy-ghost-corruption-gothic-lifestyle thing it's got going on. She doesn't know about Monstrances (assuming they're still even a thing).<br /> <br /> Ironically I suspect that <i>literally</i> stalking and killing her corrupted Solar mate would get less guff for being a &quot;creepy stalker&quot; than cautiously trying to make friends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 02-20-2019, 05:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T16:35:58-08:00","id":1290137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KittyEmpress</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290056#post1290056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elfive, your entire argument is predicated on the idea that 'Hey, being able to stalk your mate and force them to care about you back by spying on them with magic and then manipulating them into liking you back is totally cool, and great, and not at all skeevy and weird as fuck'.<br /> <br /> Like, you literally just described the grossest fucking idea of a 'Bond' I've ever heard of in any fiction I've ever read.</div> </div> </div> </div>This kind of bad faith reading makes it feel very much like actual discussion has nowhere to go.<br /> <br /> That's really what gets me about the developer response. I don't actually mind the idea of some adjustment being made, even so far as shifting it away from the exact parameters of what I like. I don't have a deep objection to a published work being not exactly as I would want it.<br /> <br /> But I find the original post to be riddled to the quick with the worst kind of bad faith reading and extreme hyperbole, and the idea that it would actually motivate a change inclined in its direction is honestly kind of depressing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":17}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T17:55:06-08:00","id":1290160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1289741#post1289741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're probably gonna do something like this in the final draft.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, did everyone forget the bit where Vance popped into the thread on PAGE TWO to confirm they're going to put something about the bond being more mutual into the final draft? <br /> <br /> Personally I don't see anything breaking either way. I'm much more concerned about the unnecessary restriction of describing every bond as originating with a &quot;political marriage&quot; when it would take one line to broaden this up to include other possibilities without disrupting the rest of the lore. <br /> <br /> It's just so sad and frustrating that this part of my character's story has been taken out of my hands for no reason. Yes, the current incarnations can relate to each other on whatever terms now, but telling the story of who your character and their mate were to each other when they first bonded so long ago (lovers, comrades, teacher and student, parent and adoptive child, enemies who became best friends) is cool and thematic and mythic and I just ... can't? Unless it's this one thing? If I want to give context to the bitter rivalry between a Lunar and her mate by hearkening back to what brought them together in the first place, I only have this one story to play with, and I don't see why. <br /> <br /> And don't come at me with that &quot;political marriages are political arrangements so you can define how the pair actually relate to each other&quot; guff. If that's the case, why are they called marriages? Historically, political marriages created/strengthened alliances that were affirmed <i>by producing children</i>. If that expectation isn't present and the two aren't romantically involved, why do I have to call it a marriage? It's not like there aren't other spiritually significant relationships you can swear an oath before the gods on. What's wrong with one line allowing those?<br /> <br /> And no, thank you, I don't want to be patted on the head and told &quot;Well if the ST says so you can have the one speshul bond that wasn't a marriage if that will keep you happy.&quot; I just want every other option that should be a perfectly valid (and would have been in previous editions, where, for all the other faults in the presentation of Solar Bond, there was no requirement that a bond-pair had been spouses at any point) to not be invalidated in the text of the book!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T18:00:22-08:00","id":1290163,"title":"","content":"You can freely say 'these people are not dating' all you want: the devs have confirmed the bond exists for the fact that the trope of destined friends/lovers/rivals is a good trope that is common in media they wanted to match. Regardless of whether you think it's built to be used to spy on who is or isn't a Solar (if that was what it was built for, uh, it's probably not great at that), the actual real life reason it's included is for star-crossed lovers across reincarnations, vicious rivalries that transcend time, and friendships that are literally eternally written in the stars. <br /> <br /> How many of those stories predicate on these concepts being one sided?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11919-kittyempress","name":"KittyEmpress","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"142"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T18:21:18-08:00","id":1290172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1289741#post1289741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're probably gonna do something like this in the final draft.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I guess that is fine. I think it would be more impactful if the Solar has to see can only instantly recognize the lunar as their bond if they see them in their true forms as their human shape, spirit shape, or a hybrid form of the two. To me this still gives the Lunars a social edge allowing them to hide while observing the Solar. It also means that the Solar only forms the bond once the Lunar has unveiled their truth to the Solar possibly in its full monstrous glory. <br /> <br /> I think this is a good middle ground that allows for more interesting stories than two people meet and instantly recognize each other. After all Lunars are also tricksters and crazed monsters of ever changing flesh so it makes sense that they could hide even from their soulmate. <br /> <br /> On the topic of the political wedding I think it is fine, to me it is less of a marriage between individual Lunars and Solars as much as a marraige between the two hosts of demigods. Much like the Asir and Vanir.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T18:24:15-08:00","id":1290177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KittyEmpress</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290163#post1290163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How many of those stories predicate on these concepts being one sided?</div> </div> </div> </div>More than none*.<br /> <br /> Mind, I don't think that there can be any version of those stories that can transcribe very directly to a game like Exalted, because even within the consideration that it's something for players to opt in to, whatever form the Bond takes can't constitute a really major infringement on story and character.<br /> <br /> I think there are game systems that can more directly model some of the most overt forms of reincarnation romance, but I don't think Exalted is one of them.<br /> <br /> That's all on a different side where I personally care about reincarnation romance only insofar as it can have elements extracted to make something that I find distinct and enjoyable to this Edition of Exalted (founded in biases formed from exposure to prior Editions of Exalted), and all of the rest discarded.<br /> <br /> Although now it's raising questions to me arising from complications related to the manner in which the books have frequently depicted reincarnation romances that had nothing to do with Lunars. Solars with other Solars. Sidereals with other Sidereals. The ghost of a Solar who keeps being frustrated that none of the reincarnations of his Sidereal wife leave behind ghosts.<br /> <br /> EDIT: * For one thing, among the range of possibilities and realisations of the trope would be stories in which two people remember a past life relationship, one of them is somewhere between &quot;yeah, it would be totally great to resume that&quot; and &quot;welp, I guess we have an obligation written in the stars to resume that&quot;, and the other is like &quot;no, that's dumb; maybe I have these memories, even that soul, but that's not me, I don't actually have or want any such feelings, and I resent the idea of some nebulous force mandating my relationships&quot;.<br /> <br /> There are a few implications for what that means for my preferences towards Lunars, but if it's a matter of comparing pedigree of sources, it's something among the contenders that could inform an element in which at least one side of that equation practices dedicated indifference towards it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 02-20-2019, 09:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T18:27:52-08:00","id":1290179,"title":"","content":"I don't think the bond needs to be automatic on both sides to have these stories.<br /> <br /> Maybe when they meet their solar, the lunar's past life memories flare and they say something that triggers the same in the solar.<br /> <br /> Maybe the lunar suddenly getting the urge to declare themselves a rival and compete with the solar will cause the solar to view them as a rival. <br /> <br /> Maybe the lunar helping the solar out will cause him to view them as a friend. Funny how that works. <br /> <br /> I don't think it's an issue because the bond does not exist in a vacuum. And since those stories are safe, I don't see a reason to ruin the possibility of <i>other</i> interesting stories that a mutual bond doesn't allow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T18:35:44-08:00","id":1290183,"title":"","content":"I <i>also</i> think that Abyssals and Infernals muddy the waters here. I don't want them taking one look at their lunar and defecting. Sure, that's a good story, but I'd like there to be a bit of legwork involved at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T18:50:16-08:00","id":1290188,"title":"","content":"Honestly, if I was going to go for stories in which something compelling comes from the experience not being felt in the same way on both sides, I'd be inclined to first look at the Second Edition portrayal of Swan.<br /> <br /> Just, given his overall demeanour, I think there's something interesting and a little bit cute in the idea that the slightly na\u00efve young man and fresh new Exalt is here faced with a legendary 2,000 year-old Lunar who is focused very intently on him because of a tumultuous relationship to his past life, and he just doesn't have any idea what to make of that. I always enjoyed seeing little allusions to that story.<br /> <br /> I kind of roll it into an overall liking of stories in which some inherited mantle of power includes some people that will hold you accountable for the actions of a past life, and you don't actually disagree with them, but you don't feel or remember the nature of that past and needing to find a way to handle it is a bit of a balancing act. Avatar: the Last Airbender sometimes did some stuff with that.<br /> <br /> \u2026 Oh snap, Steven Universe consistently does <i>huge</i> things not only with the matter of Steven struggling with the question of whether or not he's accountable for things his mother (who is basically also his prior incarnation) did, and how to handle any accountability he does accept, but <i>also</i> has a major thing of characters projecting relationships with her onto him, of which he has no memory and struggles how to handle.<br /> <br /> So, there's at least one solid example I've got to back up my somewhat more nebulous &quot;more than none&quot;.<br /> <br /> (Gems wouldn't feel that relationship with Steven through something as direct as a metaphysical bond, but it's more a matter of how Gems perceive identity and the fact that Steven is an entirely new category of being; there are characters that know he has Rose Quartz's gemstone who simply don't have the frame-of-reference for processing Steven as a distinct person from her)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T19:01:24-08:00","id":1290193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KittyEmpress</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290163#post1290163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...the actual real life reason it's included is for star-crossed lovers across reincarnations, vicious rivalries that transcend time, and friendships that are literally eternally written in the stars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except remember that you can't tell any of those stories without having a random marriage in there at some point.<br /> <br /> I mean, it'll work some of the time, but why force it?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T19:03:42-08:00","id":1290196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290183#post1290183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I <i>also</i> think that Abyssals and Infernals muddy the waters here. I don't want them taking one look at their lunar and defecting. Sure, that's a good story, but I'd like there to be a bit of legwork involved at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>We've got some really smart folks on Team Exalted with great ideas about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T19:11:04-08:00","id":1290202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KittyEmpress</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290163#post1290163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...the actual real life reason it's included is for star-crossed lovers across reincarnations, vicious rivalries that transcend time, and friendships that are literally eternally written in the stars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just as a reminder, &quot;star-crossed&quot; is not a good thing. It means that destiny itself is set against it happening.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T19:14:26-08:00","id":1290204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290202#post1290202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just as a reminder, &quot;star-crossed&quot; is not a good thing. It means that destiny itself is set against it happening.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, and the trope of 'lovers who never can be together, and always are reincarnated on different sides throughout the ages' is a classic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11919-kittyempress","name":"KittyEmpress","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"142"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T19:39:28-08:00","id":1290211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290196#post1290196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've got some really smart folks on Team Exalted with great ideas about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really wish we'd ever seen more of Five Waves Fury.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T19:44:25-08:00","id":1290214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KittyEmpress</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290071#post1290071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Regardless of what Attribute you may use to do so, stalking someone to find out everything they like and care for, so you can specifically call out the ones you also like and care for, and thus ingratiate yourself to this person you are stalking is still creepy. Whether you're lying when you tell me &quot;Hey, I see you hate slavers, I also hate slavers!&quot; or telling the truth, stalking someone through the streets of Nexus and watching him, just so you can show up at the right moment to help him fight slavers and thus make him care for you is pretty skeevy and creepy.<br /> <br /> If someone followed you through your day, took down everything you liked to eat, then made sure to ambush you at lunch and be like 'omg, you like X too, I love x!' and then excused having to do so because they felt like they had an <i>inborn, innate magical connection to you</i> that you have absolutely 0 knowledge of, wouldn't you find that creepy as hell?</div> </div> </div> </div>We are talking about a splat that regularly stalks people to learn about their life to effectively imitate them after they murder them, drink their delicious heart juice, and steal their face. Following them around so they can figure out how to make a better first impression isn't really that weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T21:59:49-08:00","id":1290239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290214#post1290214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We are talking about a splat that regularly stalks people to learn about their life to effectively imitate them after they murder them, drink their delicious heart juice, and steal their face. Following them around so they can figure out how to make a better first impression isn't really that weird.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even taking it at the very worst, I mean, just down the forum hall we have a very popular game line where killing people and drinking all of their blood is just a thing some PCs do.<br /> <br /> Fictional characters, folks. Nothing wrong with avoiding it, or requesting it not be done at a table, but this isn't a game of perfectly upright Comics Code-approved heroism, either.<br /> <br /> This is, of course, beside the point since &quot;hey, is the person who pinged my bond sense a jerk, I should ask around and watch&quot; is not remotely &quot;stalker behavior&quot;, but fairly prudent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T00:57:57-08:00","id":1290268,"title":"","content":"I'm not really too invested in this issue, but I honestly don't understand why anyone wouldn't want the Bond to be mutual. Or rather, I can easily understand not caring, but I don't get being decidedly on the 'Not' side of things.<br /> <br /> It just seems utterly obvious to me that the Bond should be mutual. The pros simply outweigh the cons. I honestly have trouble getting for what reason anyone would be against making it go both ways. I think a lot of the perceived bad faith is born from that lack of understanding, filtered through a more invested and passionate perspective than mine.<br /> <br /> I think my main thought is that it feels like the Bond (as currently written) is specifically a Lunar thing, rather than a Solar-Lunar thing. The Bond doesn't tie two semi-immortal god-heroes together, but instead ties one of them to the other. It's not about the Lunar being leashed, but rather about the overall-... Spirit of the thing, I guess. It isn't spiritually significant to a Solar in the way it is for their mate, which feels less than ideal to me.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty happy that Vance decided to go with mutuality, but wouldn't have been all that bothered if he hadn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T01:41:45-08:00","id":1290271,"title":"","content":"The 'problem' is that the Lunar Bond needs to be flexible. It's a karmic connection which should be able to encompass everything from BFF's to star-crossed eternal lovers to fated nemesis.<br /> <br /> Whether the bond is mutual or not, at the start, is moot. In fact, lets face it, the option of it being mutual is actually already on the table. See the sidebar 'Roleplaying, A Reminder', Exalted Core p. 218. Intimacies don't solely come from someone employing the social system. If you are going for the 'Eternal Lovers' option, by all means, let the Solar gain an intimacy representing a tie of love upon meeting his fated love, eyes widening as memories of their True Love across the ages flood him, because it makes sense in the story you are telling. And if you are telling a different story, well, do something else, up to and including the Solar going 'Huh? Who exactly are you supposed to be?'. No need to shoehorn this tool into something so restrictive, and I am fine with the only one being that the Lunar definitely feels something upon meeting her bondmate and the rest being up in the air.<br /> <br /> Instead, lets focus on how this could play out in actual play! I myself have fond memories of playing out the asymmetric version, starting out with bond 5 and the solar (who was a PC) actively disliking my lunar and having to work hard, really hard, for this to finally blossom into an epic romance. But I've also seen most of the other variations over the years, and that's exactly what we want right? A system that supports the telling of many different stories as possible?<br /> <br /> Perhaps a reminder of all these options and the wide range of possibilities suffices?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T01:52:59-08:00","id":1290274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290268#post1290268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not really too invested in this issue, but I honestly don't understand why anyone wouldn't want the Bond to be mutual. Or rather, I can easily understand not caring, but I don't get being decidedly on the 'Not' side of things.<br /> <br /> It just seems utterly obvious to me that the Bond should be mutual. The pros simply outweigh the cons. I honestly have trouble getting for what reason anyone would be against making it go both ways. I think a lot of the perceived bad faith is born from that lack of understanding, filtered through a more invested and passionate perspective than mine.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet I don't see what pros it being mutual has, if you want a fated mutual romance/friendship/rivalry over generations then, well, you can just have the characters both have applicable intimacies, mutter something about the Maidens having an unusual interest in a pair of souls and just get on with it. And yeah, that sounds like it could be pretty cool and I'm sure there's a Chinese saying something along the lines of 'enemies in one life are fated to be lovers in the next' which seems like it has plenty of mileage.<br /> <br /> But the Lunar bond as something other, something external and unfortunately lopsided is of much more interest to me than a truly mutual bond and immediately sparks my imagination for, to me, far more interesting stories than a more pure love across lifetimes. I like the idea of that little bug gnawing away at the pit of their stomach, someone who no matter what they can't just simply dismiss and how it could twist up a person. If I could make one change it would simply be that the Lunar doesn't automatically know it's their mate but rather they just have an unusually strong reaction to a person for not entirely clear reasons.<br /> <br /> I think, fundamentally, the difference is a result of the kinds of characters and stories people look for and enjoy. A lot of people seem to want to play great heroes and have epic victories and achieve great deeds and basically be awesome badasses, which is cool, I think that sounds like awesome funtimes. I tned towards playing screwed up losers though who can achieve great things and then proceed to wreck them in with their hubris and personal flaws. There's a reason my two favourite Lunars are Ten Stripes and Faithful Pia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25050-fodor","name":"FODOR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T02:39:10-08:00","id":1290279,"title":"","content":"Ok, lets say they make the bond work for solars exactly as it does for Lunars.<br /> <br /> What the fuck is an appropriate intimacy to gain towards a pigeon who took one look at you, panicked and flew off?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T03:16:07-08:00","id":1290283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290279#post1290279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, lets say they make the bond work for solars exactly as it does for Lunars.<br /> <br /> What the fuck is an appropriate intimacy to gain towards a pigeon who took one look at you, panicked and flew off?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an excellent question, but it's just as applicable to Lunars themselves. My Lunar's Solar Mate was sleeping at a desk when they first met. How do you react to that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T03:22:45-08:00","id":1290286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290283#post1290283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is an excellent question, but it's just as applicable to Lunars themselves. My Lunar's Solar Mate was sleeping at a desk when they first met. How do you react to that?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think that's a lot easier, 'he looks cute when he's sleeping', 'what a lazy ass' or 'I admire his confidence to be sleeping on the job so blatantly' for example. It's not uncommon for someone to fall in love with the sleeping beauty and all that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25050-fodor","name":"FODOR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T04:02:12-08:00","id":1290291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290279#post1290279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, lets say they make the bond work for solars exactly as it does for Lunars.<br /> <br /> What the fuck is an appropriate intimacy to gain towards a pigeon who took one look at you, panicked and flew off?</div> </div> </div> </div>A sudden conviction that the pigeon was up to something, which you know is irrational, but can't shake? I mean, getting to know a Lunar is confusing at the best of times. <br /> <br /> Or maybe for Solars it only triggers when you first see one of their true forms or their Tell. That way you're reacting to the &quot;real them&quot; rather than bypassing their awesome Lunar disguise mojo with your infallible soulmate-dar and consequently having to come up with an Intimacy for a stray cat or a passerby. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T04:22:17-08:00","id":1290294,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that probably would be a good way to do it. <br /> <br /> Also means you don't lose the mysterious trickster mentor angle. Everybody wins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T05:57:34-08:00","id":1290310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290052#post1290052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The bond being one way means that when it triggers the ball is in the lunar's court. There are so many interesting stories you can spin out of that leading up til the first proper meeting. Having the solar spot them in that first scene would ruin all of that.<br /> <br /> And you can have shit like three lunars hanging round with a solar, who suspects that one of them <i>might</i> be his mate. But it doesn't matter. he and his buddies are gonna fight Prasad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aditionally, even if you restrict the solar trigger to just the lunar's true forms, you're adding a risk to the lunar being in his most natural forms. Not exactly a great statement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T06:04:49-08:00","id":1290312,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but being in your true form is putting yourself out in the open anyway. I figure if it happens at all that's the best time for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T06:15:12-08:00","id":1290317,"title":"","content":"But I don't want the Solar to know he has a bond with the Lunar. What then?<br /> I mean most of the drama from the whole Swan/Lilth story was the fact she knew and he didn't. <br /> If you want the Solar to realize he has a bond, give him a memory flashback of some sort, and stick him with an minor intimacy.<br /> If you hate the bond, just ignore it, because not all Lunars have the bond, so you can make all Lunars not have the bond in your game.<br /> <br /> I guess for me, the bond works the way it is now, which gives me more options than 2nd Ed &quot;Every Solar has a Lunar mate&quot; shtick.<br /> And somehow the Solar exaltation with the way it is presented as Big Causes seems to me to be one not to recall the bond, whereas the Lunar exaltation seems to me to be the one to recall the bond, because it means more to the Lunar than the Solar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24266-aoi-cobalt","name":"Aoi Cobalt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T06:23:29-08:00","id":1290319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290310#post1290310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aditionally, even if you restrict the solar trigger to just the lunar's true forms, you're adding a risk to the lunar being in his most natural forms. Not exactly a great statement.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know that every Lunar is going to construe the possibility that their Solar might develop feelings for them as a &quot;risk&quot;. Especially since Solars don't typically have the benefit Lunars do of actually being educated about the bond and what it means. They just feel that this person is special somehow. They don't necessarily know that the Lunar also has strong feelings they can take advantage of. Also, crazy idea... some Lunars might <i>want</i> their Solar to give a damn about them?<br /> <br /> And if having a mutual connection to a Solar is something you want to avoid so strongly you'd avoid your true forms to make sure of it, why not just take the out offered by the lore and say your character has no mate? And if you specifically want to have a mate and hold all the cards upon meeting them, I'm sure there'll still be ways to do that. We haven't seen the way they'll implement mutual bond if that's what they go with, but I'm sure they won't just make it pierce all of the Lunar's efforts to mask their identity. <br /> <br /> I don't have strong feelings either way about the auto-Intimacy aspect of the bond being mutual. I'm currently storytelling a game where we had some fun ambiguity about which Lunar was the actual mate of one of the PCs, but there are fun stories you can tell the other way too. I don't really think either way has enough abuse potential to be concerning. Assholes are gonna asshole, some people will find a way to be creeps about the bond no matter what you do. As long as OP don't reprint Lunar Taming Leash or other material which encourages and supports that behaviour in the fandom, I'll be happy about the power dynamic. <br /> <br /> I'm just not going to be okay with saying that my young Solar and her adoptive Lunar parental figure were married in a previous life. I don't want to have to think about that. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T06:30:55-08:00","id":1290321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290268#post1290268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not really too invested in this issue, but I honestly don't understand why anyone wouldn't want the Bond to be mutual. Or rather, I can easily understand not caring, but I don't get being decidedly on the 'Not' side of things.</div> </div> </div> </div>*gestures vaguely to self's posts in this thread*<br /> <br /> Like, one might not agree with my reasoning, that's cool. But I only <i>roleplay</i> as an ineffable alien entity, so I think my reasoning is fairly simple to understand.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T06:32:55-08:00","id":1290323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Measure of Hope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290319#post1290319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know that every Lunar is going to construe the possibility that their Solar might develop feelings for them as a &quot;risk&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course not.<br /> But that'd still be out there. I'm talking about player perception here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T06:34:13-08:00","id":1290325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aoi Cobalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290317#post1290317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want the Solar to realize he has a bond, give him a memory flashback of some sort, and stick him with an minor intimacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this is why I'm not super-concerned if they <i>don't </i>make the instant Intimacy aspect of the bond mutual by default. <br /> <br /> I'm honestly perplexed that this is the aspect that's been so divisive.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T06:46:58-08:00","id":1290328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290323#post1290323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course not.<br /> But that'd still be out there. I'm talking about player perception here.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So you're concerned that people will be &quot;gaming the Bond&quot; based on how and when it develops, and this will distort gameplay towards what is perceived to be optimal? <br /> <br /> I'm fairly sure most people's behaviour will be more influenced by other factors, and if someone really wants to have approaching or avoiding their mate on <i>exactly their terms</i> be a major character goal then they're going to find a way to do that anyway and it isn't necessarily a bad thing. And even if everybody did it, I'm pretty sure everyone's optimal outcome would look a bit different and thus lead to different priorities and behaviour. <br /> <br /> Is there a specific scenario you can share as an example of the problem you're seeing? Because I'm not really grasping it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T07:18:35-08:00","id":1290335,"title":"","content":"Ok, I've come up with a possible compromise:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">While the solar bond shines like the noonday sun for the lunar, it's far more subtle on the solar's end. Rather than immediate recognition, the tie manifests at the end of a scene in which the lunar's nature was revealed to her. This might be by the lunar confronting her directly, or by his bearing or actions sparking dormant past-life memories. Once established it can be eroded away, but will re-establish itself in much the same manner as the lunar's tie does at the end of any scene in which the two interact.<br /> </span></div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T07:27:09-08:00","id":1290337,"title":"","content":"Seems cromulent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T07:30:46-08:00","id":1290339,"title":"","content":"*shrug*<br /> <br /> Guess it's time to retract my Lunars pledge and refuse further pledge contributions on Exalted.<br /> <br /> This is utterly ridiculous and the fact that the devs seem to be caving to it means that certain people, with very narrow views and worse arguments, are creating changes in the game.<br /> <br /> The Lunar bond is <i>optional</i> for Lunars. If you don't like the aspects of the Bond, don't take it. I know that I would be <i>furious</i> if I was playing a Solar and a Lunar player decided that <i>my</i> Solar was their object of the bond and the ST told me I now have an Intimacy to this Lunar I can never get rid of.<br /> <br /> Everyone here is focusing on the Lunar half of the bond. You know, <i>the side with the agency</i>. Has anyone noticed that the bond, from the Solar perspective, is not positive in the least? The Lunar bond allows the Lunar to do a lot of things that the Solar might not want them to do? And what do they have to fight them with? Nothing other than the base rules. The Lunar OTOH gets a LOT of tools that are improved or just do things to a Solar.<br /> <br /> The reason that the Lunar gets the Intimacy and the Solar doesn't is that the Lunar gets benefits and the Solar doesn't. The Solars cannot 'do' anything with the Bond. This is the clearest representation:<br /> <br /> Lunar = subject of the bond. They have the agency. They get the improved powers.<br /> Solars = object of the bond. They have no agency. They get nothing from the bond that the Lunar does not want to give them.<br /> <br /> Why are you trying to penalize the Solar even further?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3551-ulthwithian","name":"Ulthwithian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T07:37:31-08:00","id":1290342,"title":"","content":"So you'd be ok with it going both ways if they <i>did</i> get improved powers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T07:49:39-08:00","id":1290344,"title":"","content":"People who want a mutual bond are aware that as written EVERY solar has a Lunar partner somewhere, right?<br /> Lunar players who don't want to mess with the bond have been given the explicit option to play a Lunar that never had a bond and so can functionally ignore that part of the setting, which is good.<br /> Those who choose to play with it have then at least had the chance to make a choice about whether their character has one or not.<br /> <br /> As a Solar player with a mutual bond that choice is taken from you. Remember how people kind of hated that the Solar bond was something that every Lunar had to suffer even if it never actually came up in games in 2nd ed? It was like a shitty sword of Damocles if Damocles was a random abusive NPC your ST could drop on you at any moment for no reason and you had to care about. And how happy people were that with 100 extra Lunars it meant you had a canon reason to just go 'nope, not me guv'<br /> That's what we're talking about reintroducing in 3e with a mutual bond. For some reason. With no meaningful support for one side of the partnership beyond maybe a paragraph in a different exalts splat.<br /> <br /> That... does not sound brilliant to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25050-fodor","name":"FODOR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T07:50:23-08:00","id":1290345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulthwithian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290339#post1290339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*shrug*<br /> <br /> Guess it's time to retract my Lunars pledge and refuse further pledge contributions on Exalted.<br /> <br /> This is utterly ridiculous and the fact that the devs seem to be caving to it means that certain people, with very narrow views and worse arguments, are creating changes in the game.<br /> <br /> The Lunar bond is <i>optional</i> for Lunars. If you don't like the aspects of the Bond, don't take it. I know that I would be <i>furious</i> if I was playing a Solar and a Lunar player decided that <i>my</i> Solar was their object of the bond and the ST told me I now have an Intimacy to this Lunar I can never get rid of.<br /> <br /> Everyone here is focusing on the Lunar half of the bond. You know, <i>the side with the agency</i>. Has anyone noticed that the bond, from the Solar perspective, is not positive in the least? The Lunar bond allows the Lunar to do a lot of things that the Solar might not want them to do? And what do they have to fight them with? Nothing other than the base rules. The Lunar OTOH gets a LOT of tools that are improved or just do things to a Solar.<br /> <br /> The reason that the Lunar gets the Intimacy and the Solar doesn't is that the Lunar gets benefits and the Solar doesn't. The Solars cannot 'do' anything with the Bond. This is the clearest representation:<br /> <br /> Lunar = subject of the bond. They have the agency. They get the improved powers.<br /> Solars = object of the bond. They have no agency. They get nothing from the bond that the Lunar does not want to give them.<br /> <br /> Why are you trying to penalize the Solar even further?</div> </div> </div> </div>What caving are you referring to?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T08:00:14-08:00","id":1290348,"title":"","content":"In the second page Vance said that they're &quot;probably gonna do something like this in the final draft.&quot;<br /> <br /> Opinion seems split on how good an idea this actually is, so I don't envy his position in figuring out how to please both sides. (even if I did come up with something I'd personally be happy with)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T08:03:23-08:00","id":1290350,"title":"","content":"He can't. So judgment is to be made on what'll derivate better over the game's development, complainers be damned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T08:06:17-08:00","id":1290351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290348#post1290348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the second page Vance said that they're &quot;probably gonna do something like this in the final draft.&quot;<br /> <br /> Opinion seems split on how good an idea this actually is, so I don't envy his position in figuring out how to please both sides. (even if I did come up with something I'd personally be happy with)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And I wouldn't be happy with. Not to say your suggestion is awful, just to further highlight that satisfying everyone is likely to be difficult to impossible with this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25050-fodor","name":"FODOR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T08:06:58-08:00","id":1290352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290348#post1290348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the second page Vance said that they're &amp;quot;probably gonna do something like this in the final draft.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Opinion seems split on how good an idea this actually is, so I don't envy his position in figuring out how to please both sides. (even if I did come up with something I'd personally be happy with)</div> </div> </div> </div>Missed that thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T08:21:27-08:00","id":1290356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290335#post1290335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, I've come up with a possible compromise:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">While the solar bond shines like the noonday sun for the lunar, it's far more subtle on the solar's end. Rather than immediate recognition, the tie manifests at the end of a scene in which the lunar's nature was revealed to her. This might be by the lunar confronting her directly, or by his bearing or actions sparking dormant past-life memories. Once established it can be eroded away, but will re-establish itself in much the same manner as the lunar's tie does at the end of any scene in which the two interact.<br /> </span></div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. I had not actually considered the question of how a Solar might retain an Intimacy.<br /> <br /> Something about it having the same capacity to reassert itself feels mildly off to me, but I can't really form any kind of argument against it.<br /> <br /> By which I mean, I don't think there's any kind of valid argument against it.<br /> <br /> That being said, the point about it coming up when a Lunar's true nature is revealed to the Lunar puts me in mind of a different angle.<br /> <br /> Up until now, I've been thinking of those flashes of past life memory primarily in terms of the first meeting with the Lunar. I've not considered the possibility of them happening later, and with increasing likelihood depending on length of exposure.<br /> <br /> So say... I like the idea that for Lunars, the recognition and connection is immediate and mystical, for Solars it can depend on experience of past life memories, ranging from something persistent and compelling before the Lunar is even met, to something that triggers with a strong wash of emotion when the Lunar is first recognised, down into something that is triggered upon witnessing the Lunar doing something that is evocative of the relationship in a past life, that triggers the associated memory.<br /> <br /> I'm inclined to the idea that most Solars would experience the matter at the latter end of the spectrum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T08:24:15-08:00","id":1290357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulthwithian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290339#post1290339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*shrug*<br /> I know that I would be <i>furious</i> if I was playing a Solar and a Lunar player decided that <i>my</i> Solar was their object of the bond and the ST told me I now have an Intimacy to this Lunar I can never get rid of.</div> </div> </div> </div>That fury would be fair, but that wouldn't be on the game rules. That's a thing for players and Storytellers to resolve with one another with an eye towards collective satisfaction; if that's not the attitude at the table, I don't think that even the best rule set in existence will make for particularly good games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T08:24:52-08:00","id":1290358,"title":"","content":"Everyone with strong opinions on this seems to be assuming that it'll be implemented in a particular way that they specifically disapprove of. It's useless to speculate and spew vitriol about it when we haven't even seen the form it'll take. Honestly, this thread started with catastrophising about the bond not being mutual and then people started catastrophising about it being made mutual and now there are people on both sides panic-arguing with each other drowning out the rest who are being reasonable and trying to bridge the gap. Can this thread please take a chill pill?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T08:25:31-08:00","id":1290360,"title":"","content":"To clarify I meant when the lunar's nature was revealed to the solar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T08:32:42-08:00","id":1290362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290356#post1290356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So say... I like the idea that for Lunars, the recognition and connection is immediate and mystical, for Solars it can depend on experience of past life memories, ranging from something persistent and compelling before the Lunar is even met, to something that triggers with a strong wash of emotion when the Lunar is first recognised, down into something that is triggered upon witnessing the Lunar doing something that is evocative of the relationship in a past life, that triggers the associated memory.<br /> <br /> I'm inclined to the idea that most Solars would experience the matter at the latter end of the spectrum.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm down with that idea except that putting more emphasis on past-life memories as a factor in shaping the current relationship makes the mandatory First Age marriage even more problematic and story-choking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T08:37:06-08:00","id":1290363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Measure of Hope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290362#post1290362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the mandatory First Age marriage even more problematic</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a thought, but I don't want to make presumptions about meaning, and I don't want to wade back through ten pages of this thread.<br /> <br /> Do you mind if I ask what you mean by the bond's origin story being problematic? By which I mean, what you find problematic about it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T09:07:03-08:00","id":1290381,"title":"","content":"That's fair, it was a ways back, I'll do the wading: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Measure of Hope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1289833#post1289833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My primary problem with Solar Bond as presented is that for no reason I can discern, the text constrains all Solar-Lunar pairings to having originated with an arranged marriage, which makes me viscerally uncomfortable. That's just not very romantic. Neither is it very platonic. It's like the worst of both worlds. It just makes the story of the bond more political than spiritual. I guess the intent was to make the bond mutually consensual, and give players more agency over whether this story element comes into play for their character, which is definitely good, but the execution just presents different problems, one of which is, ironically, player agency.<br /> <br /> Maybe a lot of people won't care about the origin of their bond, and it certainly doesn't dictate how the pair relates to each other now, but what if I <i>wanted</i> to specify the origins of my reincarnating power-couple as anything other than this one narrative we've been given? What if I wanted to tell literally any other story about the relationship that led their fates to intertwine? Why are those stories off the cards? If the bond needs to be the result of a singular effort to tie the Solars and Lunars together (and I guess I don't have a problem with a peace deal being the impetus for that), why did they only decide to sanctify this alliance with marriages? I mean, what happened to all the Solars and Lunars at the time who were asexual/aromantic or just, you know, already happily married to someone else, like a mortal? Did they just not get to participate in this whole eternal-soul-union thing, even if they wanted to participate in some other way, by swearing oaths as blood-siblings or something?<br /> <br /> &quot;Sorry honey, I love you, but we gotta divorce or I'm going to miss out on having a soul-mate <i>for all of time</i>, so I'm ditching you to marry my best friend. No, we can't just swear to be BFFs. Gotta get hitched. It's a whole thing.&quot;<br /> <br /> I know it's easy to golden-rule this, but because it's so easy (ie, nothing seems to break by changing it), I don't see the reason for the restriction in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>And further in:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Measure of Hope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290160#post1290160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's just so sad and frustrating that this part of my character's story has been taken out of my hands for no reason. Yes, the current incarnations can relate to each other on whatever terms now, but telling the story of who your character and their mate were to each other when they first bonded so long ago (lovers, comrades, teacher and student, parent and adoptive child, enemies who became best friends) is cool and thematic and mythic and I just ... can't? Unless it's this one thing? If I want to give context to the bitter rivalry between a Lunar and her mate by hearkening back to what brought them together in the first place, I only have this one story to play with, and I don't see why.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically it's a needless restriction that warps the kind of past-life stories that can be told about the bond and it would be very easy to fix with one line acknowledging other sorts of oaths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T09:39:51-08:00","id":1290396,"title":"","content":"I don't think it's hard to look upon the origin story of the Bond as something that intertwined political and spiritual considerations in a manner that I think is very fitting to setting and character (I think those two facets are tied together in the setting and its history more often than they're separate), and I don't see it as mutually exclusive from romantic elements for reasons including the possibility that of the approximately six hundred Exalted who first got involved in the process, at least some of them pushed for it to take the form of a ritual marriage because they had fallen in love with each other, as well as many many cases in which romance came <i>after</i> the marriage.<br /> <br /> Which has often been the case, historically, with arranged marriages. Which <i>remains</i> the case with a lot of arranged marriage in the societies in which it is practiced. Like, arranged marriage is still heavily practiced in India, as just one example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Measure of Hope</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if I wanted to tell literally any other story about the relationship that led their fates to intertwine?</div> </div> </div> </div>Then use the Golden Rule. It's a background element, it's not a huge deal to have the idea that, in-character, there are a few variations or alternatives to the most widely repeated version of the ancient story, if one doesn't just try to get it revised wholesale for their game entirely.<br /> <br /> I think some elements of the setting are stronger when they're given an originating narrative than when they're just left up in the air. Sure, those narratives may end up bugging some people, but then just... change them.<br /> <br /> Like, you're saying it's bad because it doesn't inherently vary, so do you also dislike the Primordial War? The Usurpation? The Great Contagion? Are these things wrong to write into the books because &quot;what if X wants the origin of the Exalted to have been something different&quot;?<br /> <br /> And again, if X wants that... just do it. Like, X clearly knows what they want, they don't need the book to provide them with an origin story. It sounds more like X is looking for some kind of validation or priority to be given to their preference. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Measure of Hope</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">what happened to all the Solars and Lunars at the time who were asexual/aromantic</div> </div> </div> </div>Then whatever the language of it, it probably felt more like a pledge of fealty between liege and vassal.<br /> <br /> That and, while a lot of the setting, and virtually all of the <u>writing</u> is fairly inclusive, I don't think it's unfair for there to be characters and cultural mores in the setting that fall a bit short of the attitudes of a 21st century Western liberal viewpoint. By which I mean, I don't think it's outrageous to say that the majority of prehistoric Exalted (and humans in general) had little understanding of or care for ace people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Measure of Hope</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">already happily married to someone else, like a mortal?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I think one thing that wouldn't have happened is... anybody caring. And if anybody did, what are they going to do about it? Who is giving the Law to whom?<br /> <br /> I don't think the prehistoric humans of Creation or the authorities of Heaven necessarily gave much thought to ace people, but I also don't think they had European attitudes towards things like monogamy, or related definitions of marriage.<br /> <br /> {reads a bit further}<br /> <br /> Okay, I see you're acknowledging the golden rule element and expressing dissatisfaction with it, in which case I refer primarily back to my thought that it's worthwhile having elements of the setting that try to proactively fill in a bit of context and provide some evocative mythical or historical heft, particularly for the benefit of people who can't or don't already have their own ideas about how they'd like to fill in that space.<br /> <br /> That, and I'll also point out that current Exalted writers are still prior Exalted fans, some of the idea of ancient political marriages that recurred over lifetimes and could evolve into stronger personal bonds was how First Edition did it, and I'm fairly sure that there are people among the writers who found that take very compelling and wanted to present it and share it and put it out for new people to get a look at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T09:45:51-08:00","id":1290401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulthwithian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290339#post1290339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I know that I would be <i>furious</i> if I was playing a Solar and a Lunar player decided that <i>my</i> Solar was their object of the bond and the ST told me I now have an Intimacy to this Lunar I can never get rid of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that really a thing that happens at your table, that some people gang up and decide your character backstory for you over your own input? If so, that's not something any change to the rulebook can fix; you need to talk with those people and let them know they are not respecting you as a fellow player.<br /> <br /> No character decides who is who's bondmate. That's a player decision. Player agency will always have different constraints to character agency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T09:59:05-08:00","id":1290408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290396#post1290396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then use the Golden Rule. It's a background element, it's not a huge deal to have the idea that, in-character, there are a few variations or alternatives to the most widely repeated version of the ancient story, if one doesn't just try to get it revised wholesale for their game entirely.<br /> <br /> I think some elements of the setting are stronger when they're given an originating narrative than when they're just left up in the air. Sure, those narratives may end up bugging some people, but then just... change them.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Then why enshrine it in the background as written that all bonds sprang from a marriage? Why not include a statement that while this is how the majority of bonds came to be, some solars and lunars found a different path?<br /> <br /> What is gained by prescribing such a setting element as opposed to asking players to create their own origin of their bond?<br /> <br /> If you have to break the lore as written (no matter how allowed that is) to override a backstory element that isn't necessary for any narrative reasons, you set a precedent of having to fight the setting to get the fun you want, and that's not a good starting point to enjoying the game.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T10:11:07-08:00","id":1290412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BjornTheFellhanded</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290408#post1290408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What is gained by prescribing such a setting element as opposed to asking players to create their own origin of their bond?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Stuff... all over the rest of my post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T10:18:21-08:00","id":1290417,"title":"","content":"Marriage can literally just mean a union, of any kind. <br /> <br /> So even the bonds that weren't literally marriages were literally marriages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T10:19:18-08:00","id":1290418,"title":"","content":"You know, whatever else I think about the subject, and whatever feelings I have about communication and receptivity, I do want to say that I appreciate and admire Robert Vance's response to a complaint, both in its grace and in its willingness to consider change.<br /> <br /> I've gotten too used to developers who can get really pissy and defensive about complaints against their work. If I'm being completely honest, my initial expectation for this thread on seeing that Vance was the most recent responder was for something of that type, and I was kind of excited about that. That shaped the initial impact that the response had on me. That was wrong of me.<br /> <br /> There is no doubt in my mind that Vance not actually being that kind of developer makes this a better community, and Exalted a better game. Himself, and Eric. I would sooner that they never again write something that appealed to my tastes or captured my imagination in particular than if they were people who did, and backed it up with that kind of discourse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T10:43:29-08:00","id":1290426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290396#post1290396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, you're saying it's bad because it doesn't inherently vary, so do you also dislike the Primordial War? The Usurpation? The Great Contagion? Are these things wrong to write into the books because &quot;what if X wants the origin of the Exalted to have been something different&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not really a fair comparison, because those are all a) Not as deeply personal and b) with the possible exception of the Primordial War, not something voluntarily opted into by individual Solars and Lunars.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290396#post1290396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then whatever the language of it, it probably felt more like a pledge of fealty between liege and vassal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Slides right back into territory the devs seem to have been keen to avoid with this edition's portrayal of the bond. And you really can't think of any formal relationship besides marriage where both parties are equal? Or uneven relationships that are more personal and caring than swearing obedience to a superior?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290396#post1290396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That and, while a lot of the setting, and virtually all of the <u>writing</u> is fairly inclusive, I don't think it's unfair for there to be characters and cultural mores in the setting that fall a bit short of the attitudes of a 21st century Western liberal viewpoint. By which I mean, I don't think it's outrageous to say that the majority of prehistoric Exalted (and humans in general) had little understanding of or care for ace people.<br /> <br /> Well, I think one thing that wouldn't have happened is... anybody caring. And if anybody did, what are they going to do about it? Who is giving the Law to whom?<br /> <br /> I don't think the prehistoric humans of Creation or the authorities of Heaven necessarily gave much thought to ace people, but I also don't think they had European attitudes towards things like monogamy, or related definitions of marriage.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the narrative as it stands works perfectly if the architects of the bond were dicks to many of the people involved or affected. I mean, okay, Creation doesn't have such a thing as a perfectly un-problematic society, and nor should it, because it's hard to tell interesting stories about perfect utopias. It still feels like a sharp turn from all the encouraging signs of inclusivity that have been baked into the setting in many places this edition. I'll admit my cultural monogamy-bias was showing in the aside about divorce though. But I don't think that diminishes my main point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290396#post1290396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I see you're acknowledging the golden rule element and expressing dissatisfaction with it, in which case I refer primarily back to my thought that it's worthwhile having elements of the setting that try to proactively fill in a bit of context and provide some evocative mythical or historical heft, particularly for the benefit of people who can't or don't already have their own ideas about how they'd like to fill in that space.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely agree that filling in some mythic history to spark ideas and set the tone and provide framework is a good idea. But the specifics of how they've filled in this bit means I have to beg for a special exemption for previously valid options that have been closed off for no good reason that I can see. I don't see the utility of this restriction. No one has been able to explain it to me. You can still fill in that blank in a way that isn't so exclusionary, and that preserves the intent of the existing story, you just throw a &quot;or other similar oaths of mutual commitment&quot; in there somewhere. It's a one line fix. No one has been able to explain why the restricted version is preferable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290396#post1290396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That, and I'll also point out that current Exalted writers are still prior Exalted fans, some of the idea of ancient political marriages that recurred over lifetimes and could evolve into stronger personal bonds was how First Edition did it, and I'm fairly sure that there are people among the writers who found that take very compelling and wanted to present it and share it and put it out for new people to get a look at.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I hope there's further material forthcoming that makes it compelling for me, because as of right now, it very much isn't. And that really stands out from the fantastic material we've been seeing for Lunars otherwise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290417#post1290417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Marriage can literally just mean a union, of any kind.<br /> <br /> So even the bonds that weren't literally marriages were literally marriages.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that usage is what is intended by the text, it could do to be made a little more explicit, since it's not the one most people will assume.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":23907,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","user":"Measure of Hope","date":".  Edited to avoid double-posting. 02-21-2019, 01:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T11:08:46-08:00","id":1290435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Measure of Hope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290426#post1290426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not really a fair comparison, because those are all a) Not as deeply personal and b) with the possible exception of the Primordial War, not something voluntarily opted into by individual Solars and Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Measure of Hope</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Slides right back into territory the devs seem to have been keen to avoid with this edition's portrayal of the bond. And you really can't think of any formal relationship besides marriage where both parties are equal? Or uneven relationships that are more personal and caring than swearing obedience to a superior?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's my phrasing because I don't find the terms objectionable or weighted. I think the underlying principle is still one in which the pledged relationship can be <u>something</u>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Measure of Hope</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the narrative as it stands works perfectly if the architects of the bond were dicks to many of the people involved or affected.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the one hand, I question the &quot;many&quot; that would be involved. On the other hand... yes. The whole thing started with a war. Hell, the whole thing was done by prehistoric humans; by my perspective on what the evolution of society in the setting would be like, I would be extremely wary about having even the nicest of those people anywhere near me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Measure of Hope</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It still feels like a sharp turn from all the encouraging signs of inclusivity that have been baked into the setting in many places this edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just want to quote the actual text employed, just to make sure I'm not forgetting or disregarding some salient point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the end, the two sides made peace through a series of sacred and political marriages, forging ties between the Lunars and Solars that would persist even beyond death. </div> </div> </div>That's it. That's the entirety of what is said about the origin of the Bond. It actually strikes me as rather sterile, albeit in a manner that frees people to place whatever context on any given pairing.<br /> <br /> What is excluding about it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Measure of Hope</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to beg for a special exemption for previously valid options that have been closed off for no good reason that I can see.</div> </div> </div> </div>When were they previously valid?<br /> <br /> Ultimately, it can't be everything for everybody. The intention of my argument is more against any statement that might imply or accuse outright the subject of having no appeal to anybody, and being completely artistically void.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T11:13:23-08:00","id":1290439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Measure of Hope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290426#post1290426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I definitely agree that filling in some mythic history to spark ideas and set the tone and provide framework is a good idea. But the specifics of how they've filled in this bit means I have to beg for a special exemption for previously valid options that have been closed off for no good reason that I can see. I don't see the utility of this restriction. No one has been able to explain it to me. You can still fill in that blank in a way that isn't so exclusionary, and that preserves the intent of the existing story, you just throw a &quot;or other similar oaths of mutual commitment&quot; in there somewhere. It's a one line fix. No one has been able to explain why the restricted version is preferable.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, this might be part of the problem. The whole &quot;<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">or other similar oaths of mutual commitment&quot; bit, because I can't think of any current oaths of mutual commitment right now that isn't marriage. If there were oaths of mutual commitment that were instantly recognized as such, that term could have been used. <br /> But since &quot;marriage&quot; seems to be the only immediately recognizable term we have, that's the one that got used. </span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24266-aoi-cobalt","name":"Aoi Cobalt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T11:20:26-08:00","id":1290441,"title":"","content":"Blood brothers?<br /> <br /> Guan Yu, Zhang Fei and Lu Bei?<br /> <br /> Covenants between God and man?<br /> <br /> Feudal oaths?<br /> <br /> Though I guess while the last two are mutual, they're not equal.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T11:27:44-08:00","id":1290445,"title":"","content":"I didn't think of the blood brothers, although that gives a different gender slant than marriage.<br /> And, in my shame, I must admit to not having read Romance of the Three Kingdoms.<br /> Maybe adding blood brothers to the line about the bond in the Lunars Book would fix this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24266-aoi-cobalt","name":"Aoi Cobalt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T11:35:57-08:00","id":1290449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290435#post1290435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's my phrasing because I don't find the terms objectionable or weighted. I think the underlying principle is still one in which the pledged relationship can be <u>something</u>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290435#post1290435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is excluding about it?<br /> <br /> When were they previously valid?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a limit on a player's agency to establish their own backstory. In 2E, you were free to say &quot;My Lunar was her Solar's mentor in their first life, and when she was reborn he returned the favour. Now he's an Abyssal, and it's her turn to guide him, if she can look past what he's become&quot; or &quot;This is a friendship and rivalry that has echoed through the ages&quot; or any number of things. Now every such story has to include &quot;Er, and at some point they were married.&quot; <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290435#post1290435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ultimately, it can't be everything for everybody. The intention of my argument is more against any statement that might imply or accuse outright the subject of having no appeal to anybody, and being completely artistically void.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never accused it of being artistically void, or stated that it doesn't appeal to anyone. Hell, reincarnation romance appeals to <i>me</i>, as <i>one possible option among many</i>. I just don't see the point of dictating that you <i>have</i> to hamfist a marriage in there, even if that's not the story you want to tell.<br /> <br /> I mean maybe the story you want to tell is &quot;We're best friends with awkward memories of having been married in a past life&quot; or &quot;I cherish the memory of who she was, but can't abide the monster she's become, so for the sake of my beloved's memory I must destroy her&quot; and that's fine, that sounds fun. But mandating the inclusion of the marriage as opposed to allowing a variety of expressions of the oath within the context of the post-war sacred alliance seems to serve no purpose, and is thus, in the face of the impact on player agency, only a detriment. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T11:40:15-08:00","id":1290453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aoi Cobalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290445#post1290445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't think of the blood brothers, although that gives a different gender slant than marriage.<br /> And, in my shame, I must admit to not having read Romance of the Three Kingdoms.<br /> Maybe adding blood brothers to the line about the bond in the Lunars Book would fix this?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Gilgamesh/Enkidu tumultuous friendship is literally the first reference given for the bond in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T11:42:11-08:00","id":1290455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aoi Cobalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290445#post1290445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't think of the blood brothers, although that gives a different gender slant than marriage.<br /> And, in my shame, I must admit to not having read Romance of the Three Kingdoms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, they swear an oath under a peach tree to die on the self-same day. From then on, they're eternal brothers.<br /> <br /> Though, it's actually an inspiration for Dragonblood sworn hearths, rather than Solar Bonds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T11:53:24-08:00","id":1290464,"title":"","content":"I haven't been particularly interested in arguing about this further - I said my thing, people (even Vance!) read and acknowledged it, cool. Mission accomplished. So I'm not going to try to wade into the fray here, but I think the ongoing discussion as a whole has lost sight of the solution I posed in the OP. There's a lot of talk going around about how mutual, mechanically mandatory minor ties would ruin the Bond for some people, and how those people are incredibly disappointed that Vance said they'll be changing the Bond for that reason. That's not the change I proposed be made, and unless I'm wildly misreading the situation, it's not the change that the team are making. As I understand it, that way of working the Bond was never even an option, because OPP frowns upon it.<br /> <br /> What I suggested, and what I believe the writers are riffing off here, is removing the mechanical impact of the tie and instead leaving it a lore thing that clearly <i>should </i>have some sort of impact, but doesn't spell out exactly what that impact must be. People on both sides are getting antsy because they have cool ideas for how their vision of the Bond plays out and don't want to be constrained to a mutual Bond, or to a one-sided one. This is exactly the benefit of <i>not </i>having a specific, clear, printed right there on the page mechanical definition of what the Bond is and what it does. Give people inspiration and ideas, and leave it up to the group to figure out how exactly they want the Bond to play out at their table, for the stories they want to tell with it.<br /> <br /> Both sides can be happy here. Unless you specifically want your vision of the Bond to &quot;win&quot;, to be laid out in black and white as the only valid way to play the Bond for the rest of time, nobody loses from a more freeform implementation of it. We can actually all get what we want here. It's not a zero-sum game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T12:00:45-08:00","id":1290466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290268#post1290268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not really too invested in this issue, but I honestly don't understand why anyone wouldn't want the Bond to be mutual. Or rather, I can easily understand not caring, but I don't get being decidedly on the 'Not' side of things.<br /> <br /> It just seems utterly obvious to me that the Bond should be mutual. The pros simply outweigh the cons. I honestly have trouble getting for what reason anyone would be against making it go both ways. I think a lot of the perceived bad faith is born from that lack of understanding, filtered through a more invested and passionate perspective than mine.<br /> <br /> I think my main thought is that it feels like the Bond (as currently written) is specifically a Lunar thing, rather than a Solar-Lunar thing. The Bond doesn't tie two semi-immortal god-heroes together, but instead ties one of them to the other. It's not about the Lunar being leashed, but rather about the overall-... Spirit of the thing, I guess. It isn't spiritually significant to a Solar in the way it is for their mate, which feels less than ideal to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know.<br /> I'm not a huge fan of lots of reincarnation relationships tropes nor am I of lots of the way those tropes usually are executed and when it's reincarnation romance, most of the time, it's worse.<br /> <br /> The other problem I have with the forced &quot;everyone is mutual thing&quot; is that I think the &quot;everything's possible&quot; solution is better because I clearly don't want every solar-lunar bond in Creation being about cute but not that healthy (nor that beautiful to me) clich\u00e9 reincarnation relationships and because lots of relationship possible with the bonds I don't think as being toxic are not necessarily based on mutuality (like some of those used in tragic parental relationship).<br /> <br /> Other problems I have are those implied by the practical execution of the lunar-solar bonds and what it means in the setting. And I think that because of that, those bonds being toxic will most of the time depend on the ST goodwill rather than them being mutual or not.<br /> <br /> And all of it makes me think that the complaints are more about overestimated little problems and underestimated bigger ones for the sake of the healthiness of a specific esthetic expectation about the book rather than really caring about most players needs and sensitivity. I don't see any essential problem here, it's just that I don't see why the debate appeared as if no compromise was possible.<br /> <br /> And I'm sorry if it's hard to read. &gt;&lt;<br /> I hope it's not. =.=<br /> <br /> EDIT: It may be off topic now, I don't know. There is a huge amount of time between the moment I saw Kleptomania's message and the moment I started to write this. I had things to do in another town.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23607,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23607-roseplancton","user":"RosePlancton","date":". 02-21-2019, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23607-roseplancton","name":"RosePlancton","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T12:09:18-08:00","id":1290474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290464#post1290464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think the ongoing discussion as a whole has lost sight of the solution I posed in the OP.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry to have taken up so much space debating a problem that's orthogonal to your original post, I just didn't want to start a second &quot;Here's a problem with Lunar Bond&quot; thread. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T12:11:58-08:00","id":1290479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Measure of Hope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290474#post1290474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry to have taken up so much space debating a problem that's orthogonal to your original post, I just didn't want to start a second &quot;Here's a problem with Lunar Bond&quot; thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't mind topics drifting, that's a perfectly natural part of discussion. I just wanted to remind people that the thing they're getting upset and worried about almost certainly isn't actually happening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T12:29:56-08:00","id":1290488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290412#post1290412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Stuff... all over the rest of my post.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you rephrase it then for me, please? I don't see how 'all bonds are the result of arranged marriages' offers more than 'most bonds are the result of marriages, but others have developed over time as well' to the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290435#post1290435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is excluding about it?<br /> <br /> When were they previously valid?<br /> <br /> Ultimately, it can't be everything for everybody. The intention of my argument is more against any statement that might imply or accuse outright the subject of having no appeal to anybody, and being completely artistically void.</div> </div> </div> </div>It excludes anyone who'd rather not play a character who was married to a lunar in a past life from having a bond for their character.<br /> <br /> In 2nd ed, the lunar bond was explicitly allowed to take any form, now, it all links back to that one marriage during the first age.<br /> <br /> That's the thing about game settings as opposed to self contained stories: They have to be open enough, especially in matters of low impact, to allow players to create varied characters. Sometimes that means artistic appeal has to take a back seat to not pointlessly prescribing character decisions.<br /> <br /> After all: The bond as written means that every solar and most lunars at some point in their reincarnation cycle agreed to get married. Not 'were forced into a war' or 'were murdered in a coup' or 'had to face a plague'. Those are all things that happened to them, not choices they made. This marriage based bond means that no character that didn't CHOOSE to go through with this marriage can have a bond.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T12:34:12-08:00","id":1290490,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Measure of Hope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290449#post1290449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">In 2E, you were free to say &quot;My Lunar was her Solar's mentor in their first life, and when she was reborn he returned the favour. Now he's an Abyssal, and it's her turn to guide him, if she can look past what he's become&quot; or &quot;This is a friendship and rivalry that has echoed through the ages&quot; or any number of things. Now every such story has to include &quot;Er, and at some point they were married.&quot;</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">In Second Edition, the lore background to the Bond was the Unconquered Sun telling Luna to give it to them so that those Chosen would always be placed beneath his own, the Intimacy was something that the Lunar couldn't lose at all, and the only mechanical benefit to it was getting extra dice used to enhance service or aid to the Solar, which came with an equivalent penalty to Mental Defence Value against that Solar.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I feel as though you're getting too hung up on the origin story, and disregarding the way that multi-faceted relationships across a number of lifetimes are both inherent to what is enduring about the Bond, and will form the substance of any First Age memories. A newly reacquainted Solar and Lunar seem to me to be a lot more likely to remember the last time their Essences were together than they are to a few decades after the War of the Gods.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290464#post1290464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What I suggested, and what I believe the writers are riffing off here, is removing the mechanical impact of the tie and instead leaving it a lore thing that clearly <i>should </i>have some sort of impact, but doesn't spell out exactly what that impact must be.</div> </div> </div> </div>How far do you mean by that? Just removing the Minor Tie, or going as far as the Charm effects?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T12:39:05-08:00","id":1290493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BjornTheFellhanded</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290488#post1290488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 2nd ed, the lunar bond was explicitly allowed to take any form, now, it all links back to that one marriage during the first age.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am amazed and perplexed to see several people holding up the Second Edition Solar Bond as an example of something diverse and inviting.<br /> <br /> Like, there are other things in your post that I do have thoughts in response to, and maybe I'll work my way into them at a later point, but seeing this line being repeated has thrown me completely for a loop.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T12:51:02-08:00","id":1290497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290490#post1290490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How far do you mean by that? Just removing the Minor Tie, or going as far as the Charm effects?</div> </div> </div> </div>This: <span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">10chars</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond#post1289655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2 - Remove the mechanical impact of the Bond altogether. There is no tie. Lunars are not forced to feel anything for their Solar mate. All the fluff can remain, talking about how Solar and Lunar mates feel a strange sense of recognition when they see each other, and often leading into grand romances stretched out across lifetimes. That concept's already in the corebook, we're not adding any new, exclusive Solar content to the Lunar book here. The charm riders can remain - the corebook also, conveniently enough, has a Lunar mate charm rider, so there's clear precedent for having charm effects without a mechanical effect of the Bond itself, and the concept of the Solar mate is already very well established so it's not going to look weird to have the riders without any other mechanical enforcement of the Bond. But the magically compelled tie, the thing that sets up the Bond as being inequal right from the word go because Solars can't have it too, that has to go. Abandoning the inherently unequal mechanical implementation allows the Bond to become properly reciprocal, as it always should have been - needed to be, even. It becomes something that your group can use to whatever extent they like, in whatever way they like, developing intimacies as is appropriate to the story they tell rather than being told in black and white right there on the page that the Lunar feels something and the Solar feels nothing. It still even makes the Bond feel mechanically impactful, since even without a forced intimacy, the wide range of Solar mate riders scattered across Lunar charms makes it a Big Deal by the rules when you hang out with your mate.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T13:11:08-08:00","id":1290507,"title":"","content":"Hmmmm\u2026.<br /> <br /> I like the Tie as something with a bit of heft while barely infringing on a player or character who isn't actually running with it, but losing it while the Charms retain their incentive to find and interact with the mate would not be a disaster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T13:43:12-08:00","id":1290517,"title":"","content":"I rather like the automatic Tie. From what we've been seeing of the Lunar Charms so far, having a Tie available is beneficial to them, even desirable.<br /> <br /> Whether you want to protect what you have the Tie towards, or whether you want to destroy what you have the Tie towards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T14:05:46-08:00","id":1290528,"title":"","content":"Of course, a fated connection with no mechanical impact is already easy enough. Just mark down a custom &quot;Fated Connection&quot; Flaw (&quot;Storytellers and players should feel free to design their own additional Flaws.&quot; - Core, p. 167) on your character sheet. Which, of course, any character can take, with any origin, connecting to any relevant character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T16:06:33-08:00","id":1290567,"title":"","content":"I miss a lot when it's busy days at the office. <br /> <br /> Can I request fan art of <i>Magnificent Pigeon who Stole the Heart of the Sun</i>? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">In jest and good humor!</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T17:32:35-08:00","id":1290609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aoi Cobalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290439#post1290439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know, this might be part of the problem. The whole &quot;<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">or other similar oaths of mutual commitment&quot; bit, because I can't think of any current oaths of mutual commitment right now that isn't marriage. If there were oaths of mutual commitment that were instantly recognized as such, that term could have been used.<br /> But since &quot;marriage&quot; seems to be the only immediately recognizable term we have, that's the one that got used. </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that and in our current day, it's easy to forget that for much of history, marriage wasn't something that even spoke very much to love.<br /> <br /> The &quot;I believe in traditional marriage: unions of heirs to secure alliances among rival lords!&quot; gag, you know?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T19:08:10-08:00","id":1290627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290490#post1290490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">In Second Edition, the lore background to the Bond was the Unconquered Sun telling Luna to give it to them so that those Chosen would always be placed beneath his own, the Intimacy was something that the Lunar couldn't lose at all, and the only mechanical benefit to it was getting extra dice used to enhance service or aid to the Solar, which came with an equivalent penalty to Mental Defence Value against that Solar.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div>There's a reason I'm not holding up any other aspect of the 2nd Ed Bond as preferable, just the fact that you and your bond-mate could have whatever relationship history across your reincarnations that you wanted. But you responded to every aspect of the 2nd Ed bond that I wasn't talking about rather than addressing the one and only aspect of it I mentioned, so I don't think I'm the only one getting &quot;hung up&quot; here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T21:38:59-08:00","id":1290648,"title":"","content":"I like the angle of 'The Solar may gain a tie when they see the Lunar's true nature'. And for roleplaying it... Well, I remember a good friend of mine making a bit of advice for characters.<br /> <br /> <i>Your characters don't necessarily have the rules book in front of them</i>.<br /> <br /> You, the player, may know of this Solar Lunar Bond. You, the Solar's Player, and the ST or the Lunar's Player, will know about this Solar Bond. It's possible that the Lunar, from their mentor in the Pact, may know that some Lunars are Bonded to Solars.<br /> <br /> However, it's entirely reasonable that the Solar, in-character, has no idea what this is, if you play it as 'Receives a mutual Tie'. Could be as simple as &quot;Who was that other person in the battlefield? And why did he have such sad eyes?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T01:21:45-08:00","id":1290684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290490#post1290490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I feel as though you're getting too hung up on the origin story, and disregarding the way that multi-faceted relationships across a number of lifetimes are both inherent to what is enduring about the Bond, and will form the substance of any First Age memories. A newly reacquainted Solar and Lunar seem to me to be a lot more likely to remember the last time their Essences were together than they are to a few decades after the War of the Gods.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div>What I'm getting hung up on is the precedent in usurpation of control: As written, a decision is made by the lore on behalf of the character that the player has to accept. Romantic or not, enthusiastic or not, you are being <i>told</i> that your character made this particular life/lives changing decision to get married. When a GM/ST/DM does it, we call that railroading.<br /> <br /> Railroading can be done not-terribly, but you should only try if you have a good reason to need to. What is the reason here?<br /> <br /> I am not talking about mechanical benefits or equality, I'm talking about 'Why is a player being told what their character decided to do back then, as opposed to being asked to make up something cool themselves?'<br /> <br /> In a game that wants to embrace 'choices matter' as a core principle, there needs to be a good reason to restrict such an important choice to 'you got married' or 'you don't get to play with this story element'. What is that reason?<br /> <br /> And this is different from the Usurpation, for example, because it dictates a choice rather than a fate. The ST is expected to inflict horrible fates on the PCs, but they are also expected to not touch their agency, their freedom to make choices.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T01:31:44-08:00","id":1290690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BjornTheFellhanded</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290684#post1290684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What I'm getting hung up on is the precedent in usurpation of control: As written, a decision is made by the lore on behalf of the character that the player has to accept. Romantic or not, enthusiastic or not, you are being <i>told</i> that your character made this particular life/lives changing decision to get married. When a GM/ST/DM does it, we call that railroading.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Er, no. No you aren't. A previous owner of your exaltation made a decision, and now you need to deal with the consequences. That's not railroading. That's just how exalted works. <br /> <br /> Your character is NOT their prior incarnation. Ultimately there's no difference between the first age solars and lunars doing this and the incarnae decreeing it so, save that it puts agency in the hands of the exalted themselves, as it should be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T02:01:06-08:00","id":1290697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290690#post1290690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Er, no. No you aren't. A previous owner of your exaltation made a decision, and now you need to deal with the consequences. That's not railroading. That's just how exalted works.<br /> <br /> Your character is NOT their prior incarnation. Ultimately there's no difference between the first age solars and lunars doing this and the incarnae decreeing it so, save that it puts agency in the hands of the exalted themselves, as it should be.</div> </div> </div> </div>If course you are not the prior incarnation. You're not the current incarnation either. You are the player creating a character to play in the game, including decisions your character's past live's made that affect your current incarnation (usually in my experience, notably including whether to have a bond for example). Except this one decision of how the bond started is preset.<br /> <br /> If the lore included that every first age lunar chose to betray a trusted friend at least once, would that be as readily accepted? If the lore included that every first age lunar murdered at least one innocent person?<br /> <br /> This isn't a case of 'this terrible event befell you', but 'you chose this path, except, I chose it for you, now embrace that choice'.<br /> <br /> And I still haven't seen the answer to: What is gained for in terms of story fun by limiting the source of the bond thus? What would be lost by officially keeping it more open?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T02:24:15-08:00","id":1290700,"title":"","content":"I think you're getting way too hung up on modern conceptions of marriage. Like I said before, it just means a union. In this case, a big mystical union between a bunch of solar souls and a bunch of lunar souls. <br /> <br /> The context of those bonds is totally up in the air. Lovers, rivals, best buddies, go nuts. The only thing they need to have in common is that they were formalised in a massive sorcerous working at some point in history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T07:09:16-08:00","id":1290750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BjornTheFellhanded</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290697#post1290697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If course you are not the prior incarnation. You're not the current incarnation either. You are the player creating a character to play in the game, including decisions your character's past live's made that affect your current incarnation (usually in my experience, notably including whether to have a bond for example). Except this one decision of how the bond started is preset.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> How is it preset?<br /> If I'm playing a Solar, and don't want the bond, I tell my GM and my bonded Lunar never shows up. At all. And being a Solar, I don't recall the bond at all.<br /> If I'm playing a Solar, and I do want the bond, I tell my GM and he has the Lunar show up. <br /> If I'm playing a Lunar, and I don't want the bond, then I'm playing a Lunar who was never bonded.<br /> If I'm playing a Lunar, and do want the bond, I tell my GM and he has the Solar show up.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BjornTheFellhanded</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290697#post1290697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I still haven't seen the answer to: What is gained for in terms of story fun by limiting the source of the bond thus? What would be lost by officially keeping it more open?</div> </div> </div> </div>Since I can't find how the bond gets more flexible than it is now (only one side has to worry about it, and they have a choice to accept it or not), I don't don't see what the problem is.<br /> <br /> I guess the fix would be to bluntly just say, &quot;Back in the First Age, some Solars and Lunars Bonded in a ceremony that lasts beyond death (attached to their exaltations). If you want a Solar / Lunar bond, have one. If you don't, then don't play with one.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24266-aoi-cobalt","name":"Aoi Cobalt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T08:07:10-08:00","id":1290763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BjornTheFellhanded</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290684#post1290684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What I'm getting hung up on is the precedent in usurpation of control: As written, a decision is made by the lore on behalf of the character that the player has to accept. Romantic or not, enthusiastic or not, you are being <i>told</i> that your character made this particular life/lives changing decision to get married. When a GM/ST/DM does it, we call that railroading.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Like Elfive said, I think your main sticking point is the word marriage (or at least that's how it is coming across). If it said &quot;union&quot; instead of &quot;marriage&quot; would you have the same issue?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T13:21:59-08:00","id":1290890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BjornTheFellhanded</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290684#post1290684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What I'm getting hung up on is the precedent in usurpation of control</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't find common ground with your perspective, and I'm feeling myself sliding towards that habit that I've already slipped into in some Lunar discussion elsewhere in which I turn really caustic in that way I often instantly regret, so my continuing to argue this wouldn't be good for anybody.<br /> <br /> I like the current setup enough to not want it to change, but can't ultimately begrudge something that might bring some satisfaction to distinctly unsatisfied people.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T13:55:51-08:00","id":1290898,"title":"","content":"Ha! I just caught up with this thread. I can\u2019t believe the consternation that the word \u2018Wedding\u2019 brings up and a minor intimacy; which the book describes as not being an integral part of who the character is.<br /> <br /> I wonder how others play with the social system in their games, because a minor intimacy I have found is not a big deal. I regularly gain and degrade intimacies.<br /> <br /> Now I only played a bit of 2e, was not on the forum then, and never really cared about lunars compared to say sidereals or alchemicals so perhaps not knowing that history I sort of find this whole debate unnecessary and overly passionate. As I read the book chapters out so far the Solar bond seems like such a small part of the whole Lunar deal (and optional) that I just don\u2019t get it, so I am bowing out because it really isn\u2019t worth talking about anymore.<br /> <br /> Honestly if it wasn\u2019t for the fact it is mentioned in the core book I would recommend just dropping the whole damn concept because it really isn\u2019t all that worthwhile and no matter how the bond turns out it seems nobody is going to be happy anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T14:01:46-08:00","id":1290902,"title":"","content":"The word 'marriage' has a specific meaning, though. Sure, that specific meaning has changed, but it was always fairly specific at any given point in time.<br /> <br /> If the lore is meant to say 'some ceremony of some type', then choosing the word 'marriage' was a poor way to convey that meaning.<br /> <br /> If the only way to play a Full Moon Caste was to have been a gladiator champion in the first age, wouldn't that be needlessly restrictive? If the only way to play a Night Caste was to have been an assassin for hire, would that be fine? The words 'fighter' and 'infiltrator' would be less restrictive (but even so exclude a lot of potential for other stories).<br /> <br /> So yes, I may getting hung up on the words because I have to assume the words, and their specific meanings, were chosen for a reason.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T16:02:53-08:00","id":1290926,"title":"","content":"One of the driving points of 3e is that the details of the first age don't really matter. <br /> <br /> Maybe these marriages were romantic, maybe they weren't. It doesn't matter. It's in the past, thousands of years before your character was born. <br /> <br /> To say that this takes away agency from you is, frankly, fucking absurd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T19:09:25-08:00","id":1290960,"title":"","content":"Lunar bond-mating came from an event, whether that event was the creation of Exaltation itself (as it used to be) or some Working (which at least gets rid of the Incarna-fiat). If you're going to say that the contemporary incarnation of your character's Exaltation having been affected by that event robs the player of agency, you may as well say that the character growing up in a world with 5 poles robs the player of agency. You can decide the details of whatever effect it has on the modern character (within bounds set by the storyteller), or ignore it as having no special relevance, but unless you change the setting it's not really debatable that it happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 02-22-2019, 10:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T19:27:35-08:00","id":1290968,"title":"","content":"Said another way, details of past lives are story details, not character details. They're within player agency the same way any other story detail is. <br /> &quot;I'd like to play a game where we overthrow the Realm&quot;<br /> &quot;I think it would be fun if my urbane sophisticate suddenly got stranded in the wilderness&quot;<br /> &quot;I'm interested in telling the story of a character whose Exaltation was the only one not included in the Solar Bond (maybe because it was between lives at the time?)&quot;<br /> <br /> In other words, it's a suggestion to the Storyteller about how you want things to go, but not strictly something the player controls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T20:18:40-08:00","id":1290979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290960#post1290960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">or some Working (which at least gets rid of the Incarna-fiat).</div> </div> </div> </div>Whatever the nature of the Lunars and Solars becoming Bonded, I would see it as being beyond the power of a Working, given how those are otherwise described or inferred to interact with Exaltation. And if one is retaining the idea of Lunars having Charms with effects that are enhanced or extended by default to Solar Mates, it's definitely something deeper than what a working should effect; that's like progenitive Essence/swearing Kinship deep.<br /> <br /> I like to picture it involving the Last City on the Caul, but not necessarily. To my mind, the major component isn't any deliberately invoked magic, but the weight of the event; the significance of Lunars transferring their attention from things of the Primordial War to activity within the Realm.<br /> <br /> Actually, on that note, I do want to make one last stab at explaining why I like the Bond as it is.<br /> <br /> [And he rambled back and forth over several points in his characteristic stream of consciousness manner so much that he decided to make it a separate post]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T20:20:53-08:00","id":1290980,"title":"","content":"The Epic of Gilgamesh was brought up before, and while it admittedly made a good point about the manner in which Gilgamesh first responded to seeing Enkidu, the thing I take from that story is that Enkidu is the one on which his whole story of getting to that position has the most profound impact. The only thing that changes about Gilgamesh is that having a buddy who's up to his level makes him less of a jerk (indulge me in setting aside the whole thing of Enkidu's loss affecting Gilgamesh so deeply that he's driven to find a way to... escape his own mortality, so reverting back into being a jerk a bit). What strikes me is how, in becoming lined up for his role, the entire nature of Enkidu's being ends up changing; he goes from basically being an animal in the shape of a man (who's particularly good for digging out traps) to somebody with language, civility, a sense for living in dwellings, and engaging in human sex (possibly of the kind that affords feminine dominance, depending on exactly what was going on in ancient Sumerian civilizations). When I first heard about how the story includes a moment when Enkidu returns to the wild, but the animals all recoil from him now, signifying what he's given up and can never get back, I actually found that pretty sad, and it sticks with me a lot.<br /> <br /> When I think about the parallels that has to the origin story here, it makes me think that the Lunars were the ones who were most profoundly transformed, and I feel as though putting the majority of the Bond, for good and for ill, on their end of the equation emphasizes that.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't characterise it as letting Solars off the hook. There are still Solars who would have Gilgamesh's experience of becoming enamoured on first sight, either from the weight of memory and shared experience over lifetimes, or some intersection between the Solar's own sensibilities and how the Lunar presents themselves.<br /> <br /> But my thoughts also go to the Lunar who doesn't immediately form their side of the connection, and has it shaped by the manner in which they're connected to a Lunar whom they can't get shot of if the Lunar doesn't want to.<br /> <br /> Looking at the Gilgamesh background and some of the imagery it informs, I'm thinking of a whole thing where the Solar quality is a lot more inviolate when compared to the Lunar (the transition to Abyssal and Infernal being its own huge thing). It leads me into a narrative of... not any particular Solar character, rather the Solar ethos, having not quite known what it was getting into in making that connection with Lunars.<br /> <br /> So part of the value I feel in the Solar side not as intrinsically having the feeling is that it's the Essence thinking that it can get away with not caring about the connection and the old oaths, and the Lunar side laughing at the conceit of it.<br /> <br /> Yesss\u2026 there are a few reasons I like using the word &quot;marriage&quot;, but forget about that for a moment, think of the originating event and ceremony more on the whole as a union, an alliance. Something in which the Solar side pledged to do or give <u>something</u>. Something from which you got some Bonds that, reincarnated over thousands of years and dozens of lifetimes, never managed to be romantic, or friendly, or even necessarily a rivalry. More business. More the thing that the Lunar felt was keeping the Solar on their toes.<br /> <br /> I think there's value to the narrative of a Solar that doesn't form an Intimacy and feels aloof about the whole thing, and being connected to a Lunar who feels impelled to disabuse them of that notion.<br /> <br /> I will grant that it feels like situations where the Bond persistently and distinctively entailed a very intimate connection should only be a minority of those aloof scenarios. Not absent completely, I've already elaborated on some ways in which I value it.<br /> <br /> A basic rule of thumb that comes to my mind from having written all this (it once again being a case where my thoughts got away with me upon starting what was intended to be a simpler post) is that if one envisions the background as having been one in which the immediate prior incarnation, and a distinct number of the overall, is something in which the connections developed beyond Minor (keeping in mind that a Minor Tie can still entail an important life-long relationship), then reacquaintance kindles a feeling strong enough to form a basic Tie for the Solar.<br /> If it didn't, then the living Solar's experience of the old memories is more distant and clinical, and nothing comes out of it.<br /> <br /> All still coming from the idea that it wasn't the deep transformation for ancient Solars that it was for Lunars.<br /> <br /> And oh Lord I am looking back at all of that and feeling as though the strongest argument against making something about that mandatory for Solars is that it's a lot of baggage to process. I am thinking of it particularly from the perspective of Solar games, which as presented in the corebook do not heavily concern themselves with the baggage of old relationships to Lunars.<br /> <br /> I find that the baggage of the Lunars' old relationships to Solars is easier to write into their part of the setting, because it's part of the foundation in which their persons and culture has existed for the past 1000+ years. But like, imagine introducing somebody to the Solar Exalted, and saying that in addition to the whole general thing of being righteous heroes returned to save a world from a time of tumult in the face of a vast hostile empire, they've got to bear the intricacies of ancient relationships to Lunars.<br /> <br /> Or, if you don't introduce that in the core, it's a thing that gets introduced to them after the fact in the book of an entirely different Exalted group?<br /> <br /> I think some of these arguments need to allow a lot of concessions to the basic gameplay function of the Solars as the core Exalted.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm gonna stop right here, because otherwise I'm liable to ramble on about every other possible angle on this thing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T18:52:20-08:00","id":1291368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aoi Cobalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1290750#post1290750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess the fix would be to bluntly just say, &quot;Back in the First Age, some Solars and Lunars Bonded in a ceremony that lasts beyond death (attached to their exaltations). If you want a Solar / Lunar bond, have one. If you don't, then don't play with one.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>And what would be so wrong with that solution? That's literally all I'm asking for, but everything I've said (and what Bjorn has said) has been misconstrued every which way. It's tiresome. <br /> <br /> Don't play cute games with &quot;marriage meant a different thing back then&quot;. Everybody knows what the word &quot;marriage&quot; will be read as by most readers. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T20:13:55-08:00","id":1291407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Measure of Hope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1291368#post1291368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everybody knows what the word &quot;marriage&quot; will be read as by most readers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, I feel as though describing them as political marriages adjusts that expectation to a not unreasonable degree.<br /> <br /> If there was a change in word choice, my vote would be for a qualifier such as ceremonial or symbolic, that emphasizes them as not constituting literal marriage as being between romantic partners.<br /> <br /> I'll note that, in the absence of any description of how the individual pairings were assigned, there's nothing actually proscribing how one defines the relationships of one's first bonded incarnations. Saying that your particular subset of two people within the greater movement first connected from the Lunar opting to &quot;fight&quot; the Solar with a lot of instructive trickery, and the Solar ultimately finding that they actually benefited a lot from what that humiliation and sabotage revealed to them, so that when Merela and her Mate called for everybody to pick a buddy before the whole thing was consecrated, those two seemed like a natural choice... that's not actually grating against anything in the origin story. I'd say one has more latitude to say that's how their first incarnations met and connected than the story saying that they were hooked up before anybody was even incarnated.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T21:37:58-08:00","id":1291423,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm definitely digging the choice aspect, I wish the choice wasn't opened up in that way only to be immediately constrained in another. Because the pair you described seem just as likely to opt for a platonic oath as a marriage as we would understand it. <br /> <br /> And what all this back and forth about the nature of political as opposed to romantic marriages misses is that although they weren't necessarily (and often weren't) romantic, they were almost always sexual, because a union like that is expected to produce &quot;natural born&quot; children to seal the deal. Now, this stipulation doesn't seem like it would apply to a union of nigh-immortal god-kings, but that just begs the question of why use the same term at all unless that's how the pair choose to characterise their relationship?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T22:54:22-08:00","id":1291434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Measure of Hope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1291423#post1291423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I'm definitely digging the choice aspect, I wish the choice wasn't opened up in that way only to be immediately constrained in another. Because the pair you described seem just as likely to opt for a platonic oath as a marriage as we would understand it.<br /> <br /> And what all this back and forth about the nature of political as opposed to romantic marriages misses is that although they weren't necessarily (and often weren't) romantic, they were almost always sexual, because a union like that is expected to produce &quot;natural born&quot; children to seal the deal. Now, this stipulation doesn't seem like it would apply to a union of nigh-immortal god-kings, but that just begs the question of why use the same term at all unless that's how the pair choose to characterise their relationship?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably because the end goal was meant to be the same even if the method was different. The normal method political marriages went with was the idea that the resulting offspring would be their parent's heir with that assurance and continuation being meant to assuage further conflict. Plus it was tying chunks of people's souls together for all eterinity, calling it a &quot;union&quot; was just going to be viewed as a weird choice when it could just be called a marriage; and calling it an alliance wouldn't have seemed strong enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T00:09:35-08:00","id":1291444,"title":"","content":"B-l-o-o-d b-r-o-t-h-e-r-s","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T02:28:26-08:00","id":1291463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Measure of Hope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1291444#post1291444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">B-l-o-o-d b-r-o-t-h-e-r-s</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there a more gender neutral term for such a concept?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T02:32:12-08:00","id":1291465,"title":"","content":"Sworn-siblings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T02:35:15-08:00","id":1291467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1291465#post1291465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sworn-siblings?</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this one.<br /> <br /> Was trying to think of a punchy gender-neutral version but all I had was &quot;blood-siblings&quot; which just sounds like you're related. The only reason blood-brothers doesn't sound that way is because it's an established idiom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T04:29:37-08:00","id":1291495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1291465#post1291465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sworn-siblings?</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean like Dragon Blooded?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T04:35:14-08:00","id":1291496,"title":"","content":"Honestly there's probably at least one in-universe theory that the solars and lunars got the idea from them. <br /> <br /> Which may make some lunars all the more distrustful of it now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T05:52:42-08:00","id":1291507,"title":"","content":"Looking at a lot of the legacy of political marriages, I feel as though the most important thing wasn't necessarily the status of the heir. Sure, marriages were legitimised by consummation and producing children, but that was kind of the case with just about any marriage. A lot of times, heirs to multiple kingdoms were actually rather undesirable, because they could complicate already fraught lines of succession, and the idea of unifying multiple polities in one person was often unwanted within (you don't want to suddenly find yourself ruled by a foreigner) and without (you don't suddenly want half the continent to be unified) I think that, a lot of the time, the important thing was that it made the monarch of the other polity count as your sibling or parent; the original meaning of &quot;in-law&quot; was that, in the eyes of the law, your relationship is equivalent to a blood tie. So it would often play off of cultural attitudes towards kin loyalty.<br /> <br /> Still, that's the side coming at it from a largely patriarchal angle; I think that an often overlooked element is the union of power with your actual spouse. Eleanor of Aquitaine was the most eligible bachelorette of 12th century Europe because she carried her own authority over a sizable and wealthy duchy into her marriages. The political quality of Isabella of Castile marrying Ferdinand of Aragon was them both being supreme in their respective territories, and able to command them mutually in alliance, to fulfil their shared spiritual and territorial goals of driving Muslims out of Iberia (although the two also seem to have been genuinely into each other, and Isabella's marriage choice was actually made against a lot of powerful domestic sentiments, for a number of political reasons). <br /> <br /> You can also get things that go even more symbolic. Something I've found intriguing since I first learned of it was surviving correspondence between the rulers of civilizations of the Levant from around three to four thousand years ago (like the Egyptians and Hittites) in which they would address each other with family epithets even in cases where they weren't tied together by actual marriages, which I think might say something about what those societies thought about family relationships and the common status of their rulers.<br /> <br /> Hell, while I wouldn't find it reasonable to expect it of everybody, I would be inclined to look at the description of the binding of Solar and Lunar Exalted as a marriage as being an insight into some very different and intriguing conceptions of things such as gender roles, family relationships and the institution of marriage, not least because you're talking about humans at the beginning of their civilization; an institution of marriage might still be a fairly new thing to them.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, I'm thinking of marriage being a term ascribed to it later in the First Age, in which the narrative and people's conceptualisations are inclined to see it in terms of contemporary civilization, much as a lot of historical myth and fiction has tended to picture people living a very long time ago as basically looking and dressing and organising identically to themselves. I'm picturing this being a case even for a lot of Exalted who actually lived back then, mostly because I'm inclined to picture a two thousand year old Exalt halfway through the First Age less like a cave person enduring amidst a heavily developed society, and more like middle-aged to elderly Jack Donaghy, who by this point has been fabulously wealthy for more than half of his life and left his impoverished childhood far behind him, and his ignorance of things like basic grocery shopping is a symptom of either having grown extremely out of touch or an affectation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T13:45:38-08:00","id":1291596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Measure of Hope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1291467#post1291467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this one.<br /> <br /> Was trying to think of a punchy gender-neutral version but all I had was &quot;blood-siblings&quot; which just sounds like you're related. The only reason blood-brothers doesn't sound that way is because it's an established idiom.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So, just to be clear, you're saying you don't like the term &quot;political marriage&quot; because you want it to be clear that the relationship could be platonic, but you don't see any issues with labeling it as &quot;sworn siblinghood&quot; despite the fact that it can be a romantic relationship?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/91-wandering","name":"Wandering","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar91_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T21:30:43-08:00","id":1291716,"title":"","content":"No, not at all. I'm fine with it being either, as long as it <i>can</i> be either. My problem is being excluded from possible choices, so prescribing a different type of bond to the exclusion of other types would just be the exact same problem again and I'd be just as against it.<br /> <br /> If you actually read what I've been saying repeatedly for about 10 pages now, my problem is with it being <i>only</i> marriages. If it was &quot;sacred unions such as marriage&quot; or &quot;marriages and other spiritual unions&quot; I wouldn't have a problem. <br /> <br /> Is that FINALLY clear to everybody?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T22:49:06-08:00","id":1291727,"title":"","content":"Okay... okay, I've had a moment of clarity now.<br /> <br /> Absent all other context and background with the setting or discussion of it, even with consideration for political marriages not being strictly romantic, imagining it through the eyes of an entirely new person... yeah, the first impression would absolutely be that it consisted of putting people together in heteronormative pairings. Maybe familiarity with the setting as a whole might incorporate homosexual pairings, but for a person who has no reason to not just take the words at face value (as any before or after might be)\u2026 yes, I see it now. Even if not romantic, even if not sexual, it does intrinsically connote a kind of... domestic situation.<br /> <br /> And I can imagine ways in which that might colour the Bond in play; that even if the character creation says that the emotional content and function of the relationship varies, if the first impression is that it was a marriage and the contemporary ones constitute a kind of deviation...<br /> <br /> I know this is all kind of stating the bleeding obvious, I'm just getting it all straight in my head.<br /> <br /> I'm still attached to the term, but right now I feel as though it ought to come at the end of a sentence or two that clarifies the set up a bit; lays out a scenario of Exalted of varying kinds of relationship being matched up, and the resulting consecration and union for peace being a highly ceremonial kind of marriage (even if many treated it more literally).<br /> <br /> Before I said that it doesn't <i>not</i> say those could have been the starting relationships. The obtuseness of that stands out to me now. A scenario like this does seem like one in which it's beneficial, if not necessary, to proactively say what it is.<br /> <br /> Again for the sake of not colouring perceptions towards the Bond that has a more hostile context constituting a multi-incarnation marriage that has become estranged, rather than &quot;this kind of relationship has been typical, or even the norm, across their history&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T23:54:55-08:00","id":1291734,"title":"","content":"I think it is very much intended for Lunars to have a variety of different relationships with the Solars that they have a Bond to. Some could be sworn political or romantic marriages (whether heterosexual or homosexual, there are a LOT of examples of homosexual romantic pairings between mythical figures, especially in Greek and Chinese mythologies), they could be sworn blood brothers/sisters, or they could even be positions of fealty of a Lunar taking a role as a sworn knight, guardian or protector.<br /> <br /> And in all of these situations, there is a simple thing that is common with them all. The Vow they took.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T00:06:50-08:00","id":1291735,"title":"","content":"Thank you for giving what I have to say a fair hearing, Isator Levi. I've appreciated the clarity of your arguments throughout this discussion, and they've helped me refine my point, even if I've been a bit short with a few people in the thread recently due to the frustration of having to repeat myself for people who only heard half the conversation...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1289655-please-please-fix-the-lunar-bond?p=1291734#post1291734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it is very much intended for Lunars to have a variety of different relationships with the Solars that they have a Bond to. Some could be sworn political or romantic marriages (whether heterosexual or homosexual, there are a LOT of examples of homosexual romantic pairings between mythical figures, especially in Greek and Chinese mythologies), they could be sworn blood brothers/sisters, or they could even be positions of fealty of a Lunar taking a role as a sworn knight, guardian or protector.<br /> <br /> And in all of these situations, there is a simple thing that is common with them all. The Vow they took.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why it should be made clear that that vow does not necessarily constitute a partnership of one type for every pair to the exclusion of other possibilities. This is not something that is currently clear in the text, even if it's the intention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}